{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e","id":824985,"title":"Multi-Kith Merit in 2E?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-06T10:24:01-08:00","id":824985,"title":"Multi-Kith Merit in 2E?","content":"Would the Multi-Kith merit from the first edition of Changeling be appropriate for the second edition, given the maleable nature of the kiths? I ask because, the more I look at the prospective list of kiths we have been shown already, the more I want to make a Changeling with the Airtouched effects but more in terms of physical prowess, with their keeper having been wanting them to either entertain them fighting &quot;monsters&quot; like a television show costumed hero. Problem is, that description also matches the Playmate kith, which I would also enjoy having for this Changeling.<br /> <br /> Do note, I'm not asking if this merit will be included, more if it should be included. Part of why the Multi-Kith merit was effective in 1E was at how relatively minor the effects of the kiths were, whereas those effects are more pronouned in 2E (Chimeras in particular have powerful utlity no matter which gameline they're in for having a pronounced ability to negate supernatural effects on them, and Gravewrights have power over ghosts to rival Sin Eaters).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T10:36:46-08:00","id":824996,"title":"","content":"IMO if the Multi-Kith Merit is too good under the current scheme, simply up the price. I bet you it will stop sounding that good if it's like 4 or 5 dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T11:22:18-08:00","id":825019,"title":"","content":"New Kiths encourage to create your own - Want &quot;fire elemental&quot; character, not &quot;fire heart&quot;? Take Levinquick lightning Blessing and just change it in to fire related one. The Kiths preview <i>literally</i> say this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ED Kith Preview</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">One player might wish to play a changeling with a thunderbird kith that was identical to the ifrit kith, except the thunderbird appears birdlike and has abilities related to electricity rather than fire. Another might wish to play a phoenix kith that emphasizes how swiftly fire can move and so possesses the same blessing as the levinquick kith.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T11:28:26-08:00","id":825021,"title":"","content":"It's been stated in an earlier thread that the Dual-Kith Merit was in the version of the Merits section that went out to playtesters. Dave said he wasn't sure if it would be in the final product, or what it would cost, it would depend on how it worked out in the playtests.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think it should be included. Dual Kiths are cool, and I like cool things. I don't know what it should cost, but that part isn't as important to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T11:40:52-08:00","id":825027,"title":"","content":"Didn't see anything in the redlines saying it should be removed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T11:50:49-08:00","id":825034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=825021#post825021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I think it should be included. Dual Kiths are cool, and I like cool things. I don't know what it should cost, but that part isn't as important to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Off topic, but that pretty much sums up my philosophy of gaming, I think. Cool things are cool, don't sweat the small stuff. I wouldn't go so reductive as to say there's no such thing as bad game design (there reeeeeeeally is), but whenever I see people having some absurd conversation about the logical extreme that *could* happen with some game bobble if the players are assholes, I'm like &quot;Yeah, but it can do the cool thing. Maybe don't be jerks?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T12:02:35-08:00","id":825041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=825034#post825034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Off topic, but that pretty much sums up my philosophy of gaming, I think. Cool things are cool, don't sweat the small stuff. I wouldn't go so reductive as to say there's no such thing as bad game design (there reeeeeeeally is), but whenever I see people having some absurd conversation about the logical extreme that *could* happen with some game bobble if the players are assholes, I'm like &quot;Yeah, but it can do the cool thing. Maybe don't be jerks?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Same. And in fact, I learned that attitude by playing (and running) CofD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-06-2016, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T12:25:11-08:00","id":825054,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'd make it expensive to buy, or cheap but with a drawback of some kind. Still, the general trend of 2e has been a power increase across the board under the guideline that STs and players should be enabled by the rules, not corralled by them, so as long as it costs <i>something</i>, I don't see a huge reason to remove it.<br /> <br /> If it's an aesthetic thing, then I'd just make a new Kith, as wyrd pointed out. If you want a second Blessing, then you should have to get a Merit. Not sure I'd call it &quot;multi-Kith&quot;; I'd emphasize the fact that it's the Blessing you're getting, and like everything else, you need to justify it with some aesthetics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T13:24:53-08:00","id":825074,"title":"","content":"Well remember, Kith in 2e is &quot;how your Keeper changed you&quot; as opposed to Seeming which is &quot;how you changed yourself.&quot; If a character was made into a doll, Manequin is an obvious choice of Kith. But if that doll was used as a plaything for a childlike Keeper, it might also be appropriate for them to have the Truefriend Kith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T14:29:58-08:00","id":825099,"title":"","content":"Whatever the final cost is, I'm going to have my NPC version of Ziggy pick up Gremlin as his second kith. He went on a quest to get it as a means of emphasizing his glitched nature. I read up on the God Machine recently, and decided it'll exist in my chronicle, and Ziggy sabotaged a piece of it to get his Gremlin power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T14:58:05-08:00","id":825107,"title":"","content":"Thanks for weighing in guys, it's very much appreciated. I do appreciate that making another kith would probably be a good alternative to having two separate kiths/blessings; I'm just not sure aside from Airtouched, what would fit a changling <a href=\"http://vignette1.wikia.nocookie.net/kamenriderds/images/3/3e/Chalice.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20120527200946\" target=\"_blank\">with this kind of appearance</a> (I'm a Kamen Rider fan).<br /> <br /> The more I think about it, the more I feel that having a multi-kith merit in 2E would require having a higher Wyrd than normal. Given that one blessing/kith changes a changelings inherant being, two blessings/kiths would likely change them even deeper, as though they were implanted with more of their keeper's power/effort. Alternatively, giving them a bane of some kind may work, to show how the merger may have an inherant weakpint of some kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T18:36:25-08:00","id":825183,"title":"","content":"The problem with requiring high Wyrd as a gate, is that since Kith is supposed to reflect what happened in your Durance, you're basically forcing people into putting a huge amount of Merit dots into raising Wyrd and getting the Merit, since it makes the most sense at start.<br /> <br /> I don't know what the final version might look like, but given how much more potent the Kith Blessings are already, I'd rather something where Dual Kith grows with Wyrd rather that require it. I would do something like having neither Kith Blessing express fully (most have multiple effects) at Wyrd 1, and then as Wyrd goes up more aspects express until you hit high enough to get the full benefits of both Kiths (or maybe even more than that).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T21:26:19-08:00","id":825247,"title":"","content":"I more base that off of the original merit, which had a 2 dot and a 3 dot version; the 3 dot version required Wyrd 3 to get the ability to take a kith that wasn't part of the same seeming as the one the Changeling was, whereas the 2 dot version only allowed another kith from within the same seeming. Since the seemings now apply to all kiths, that makes the 2 dot version redundant, which leaves the 3 dot version. With 2E, I do feel that 3 Wyrd may be a bit tall, but maybe Wyrd 2 would be a decent trade-off?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T21:31:52-08:00","id":825249,"title":"","content":"We want the Dual Kith merit available for people right off the bat as an option for fun and more complex stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T21:42:02-08:00","id":825253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=825249#post825249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We want the Dual Kith merit available for people right off the bat as an option for fun and more complex stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that is definitely good to hear. It does leave me a tad confused though, because I read that the merit could only be taken at character creation...and yet it still had 3 Wyrd as a pre-requisite for the 3 dot merit. Still, thank you for elaborating Arcane. :-) Can't wait to see how Changeling 2E turns out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T21:47:40-08:00","id":825256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=825253#post825253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does leave me a tad confused though, because I read that the merit could only be taken at character creation...and yet it still had 3 Wyrd as a pre-requisite for the 3 dot merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>You read the Merit wrong; the Rites of Spring version is a two or three dot character-creation-only Merit with no Wyrd prerequisite and the Winter Masques version is a three dot Merit with a Wyrd prerequisite of 2 and no listed restriction to character creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T22:00:09-08:00","id":825264,"title":"","content":"Well, that's quite enlightening. Thank you Satchel. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T08:18:13-08:00","id":825420,"title":"","content":"Honestly, Dual-Kith is pretty balanced at 4 dots. At three dots it's just plain amazing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T08:54:32-08:00","id":826014,"title":"","content":"personally, i'd like to see it included in 2e. i tend to come up with complicated characters who tend to fall into the dual-kith region. (such as a wolf who was forced to run endlessly and eat poisoned plants)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1798,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1798-nameandverb","user":"NameAndVerb","date":".  edited for redundancy 02-08-2016, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1798-nameandverb","name":"NameAndVerb","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1798_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T09:09:44-08:00","id":826022,"title":"","content":"I tend to like Dual-Kith because it allows me to append Snowskin to anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T11:23:15-08:00","id":826085,"title":"","content":"Even with the idea of kith being how the Keeper changed you, I still love the idea of allowing the Dual Kith merit, and I'm glad it's coming back. It obviously allows for characters who were two things under their Keeper, but also can be used as an act of reclamation for oneself after character creation - adapting what the Keeper did to you in a new way and thus generating/developing a new Kith for it.<br /> <br /> Should be fun to see the combos people come up with in either case!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T14:51:24-08:00","id":826305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EndlessKng</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=826085#post826085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even with the idea of kith being how the Keeper changed you, I still love the idea of allowing the Dual Kith merit, and I'm glad it's coming back. It obviously allows for characters who were two things under their Keeper, but also can be used as an act of reclamation for oneself after character creation - adapting what the Keeper did to you in a new way and thus generating/developing a new Kith for it.<br /> <br /> Should be fun to see the combos people come up with in either case!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm essentially using it as a means of symbolic defiance. Some exchange their kith for a different one of their choice, and others take up an additional kith as a means of expressing the sort of person they want to be. Ziggy started out as a Gameplayer, representing his game development skill and logical thought. He picks up the Gremlin kith as a means of cementing his status as a living glitch and techno-mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T03:50:31-08:00","id":826687,"title":"","content":"I dig Dual-Kithing, so I'm hoping it remains, as well. But the rest of this game is really good, believe me!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T09:00:54-08:00","id":826862,"title":"","content":"Considering how varied the kith are and how changeling is supporting customization I certainly hope you can multi-kith.<br /> <br /> I hope if Dual-Kith is allowed that there will be maybe a way to get more, if that's what you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","user":"ReshyShira","date":". 02-09-2016, 12:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T12:47:18-08:00","id":827006,"title":"","content":"My big concern with Dual-Kithing is that in 1e it got too &quot;essential&quot; to making the character you want. The 2e spoilers for Kiths have them far more flexible. They're not attached to Seemings, they've got enough different powers that mixing two together can be done without a Merit.<br /> <br /> In 2e, getting two full Kith Blessings is pretty damned powerful, and less important to trying to get the fluff/mechanical stuff you want. I really don't want to see it turn into either &quot;too expensive to take unless you really really need it for a concept,&quot; or, &quot;too cheap to ever pass up because of all the boosts it gets you nothing else can come close to.&quot; Finding a balance between those with the 2e spoilers seems hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T12:49:49-08:00","id":827009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827006#post827006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My big concern with Dual-Kithing is that in 1e it got too &amp;quot;essential&amp;quot; to making the character you want. The 2e spoilers for Kiths have them far more flexible. They're not attached to Seemings, they've got enough different powers that mixing two together can be done without a Merit.<br /> <br /> In 2e, getting two full Kith Blessings is pretty damned powerful, and less important to trying to get the fluff/mechanical stuff you want. I really don't want to see it turn into either &amp;quot;too expensive to take unless you really really need it for a concept,&amp;quot; or, &amp;quot;too cheap to ever pass up because of all the boosts it gets you nothing else can come close to.&amp;quot; Finding a balance between those with the 2e spoilers seems hard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demons get Terrible Form, and that's a MASSIVE upgrade for 4xp. Why is allowing changelings something similar bad?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T18:55:15-08:00","id":827257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827009#post827009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Demons get Terrible Form, and that's a MASSIVE upgrade for 4xp. Why is allowing changelings something similar bad?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/217778-inspiration-from-demon?p=218544#post218544\">Oh for fuck's sake not again</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T19:03:03-08:00","id":827261,"title":"","content":"That's kind of a No True Scotsman question.<br /> <br /> I never said allowing a potent booster Merit was bad. I said I'm considered with the balancing act specific to Changeling Kiths and the Dual-Kith Merit.<br /> <br /> Comparing Terrible Form and Kith bonuses is also an extremely large apples &amp; oranges thing. Demonic Forms have very high costs just to access (either in Cover if you Go Loud, or in Aether and time if you're selecting from your list). Kith Blessings default to being always available to you. Demonic Forms naturally gain more abilities as Primium goes up. Kith Blessings don't get more abilities as you raise Wyrd (so far anyway, the evolution mechanics from 1e haven't been addressed yet). Demonic Form abilities are generally static boosts that don't scale with Primium or get boosted with Aether points. Kith Blessings generally either scale with Wyrd or can be boosted with Glamour. And the big thing that is hypothetical is that Terrible Form is good without being optimal. I find it very hard to imagine with Demon that you're going to be sitting there at creation and going, &quot;Man, I completely screwed myself by not taking aspect X for my form, I wish I had bought Terrible Form.&quot; You can change your aspects, and you can get more as you grow without the Merit. What I don't want to see are players that don't take Dual-Kith to feel like their character's are chumps for passing on it in favor of other things; which was one of the bigger issues my experiences with CtL 1e had regarding the Merit.<br /> <br /> Frankly, the XP cost is unlikely to be the totality of any issues I might have with the final form of Dual-Kith assuming it makes it into CtL 2e. Expensive/cheap doesn't just have to mean XP costs. Requirements, drawbacks, and so on all matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T19:58:57-08:00","id":827276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827261#post827261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Comparing Terrible Form and Kith bonuses is also an extremely large apples &amp; oranges thing. Demonic Forms have very high costs just to access (either in Cover if you Go Loud, or in Aether and time if you're selecting from your list). Kith Blessings default to being always available to you. Demonic Forms naturally gain more abilities as Primium goes up. Kith Blessings don't get more abilities as you raise Wyrd (so far anyway, the evolution mechanics from 1e haven't been addressed yet). Demonic Form abilities are generally static boosts that don't scale with Primium or get boosted with Aether points. Kith Blessings generally either scale with Wyrd or can be boosted with Glamour. And the big thing that is hypothetical is that Terrible Form is good without being optimal. I find it very hard to imagine with Demon that you're going to be sitting there at creation and going, &quot;Man, I completely screwed myself by not taking aspect X for my form, I wish I had bought Terrible Form.&quot; You can change your aspects, and you can get more as you grow without the Merit. What I don't want to see are players that don't take Dual-Kith to feel like their character's are chumps for passing on it in favor of other things; which was one of the bigger issues my experiences with CtL 1e had regarding the Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can assume your full demonic form without going loud. It gives you a +4 to rolls for partial transformations <b>and</b> increases your options dramatically. I have yet to make a demon that didn't have that merit. Why? Because it's both <b>fun</b> and <b>effective.</b> All the players that I've seen playing demon take that merit, every single one.<br /> <br /> But I digress, you're concerned about Kith abilities, and looking at them there's a few things. First off is that not all of them scale, second off is that they're still relatively minor abilities in the greater scheme of things, third off is that they are so many options that it's not about missing something vital but having an opportunity to add something new and flavorful. If there's any one single kith ability out of a hundred that becomes an absolute necessity then it's probably too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","user":"ReshyShira","date":". 02-09-2016, 11:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T20:46:44-08:00","id":827293,"title":"","content":"The problem is, essentially, your third point. You don't have to miss anything. Custom Kiths are entirely meant to be a thing, and adjusting existing Kiths to suit what your concept is, is already a thing.<br /> <br /> Basically, if you were trying to &quot;sell&quot; me on Dual-Kith, you'd be failing completely, because your core argument is, &quot;Dual Kith is how you make new and flavorful characters,&quot; which amounts to, &quot;failing to take Dual-Kith makes your character a chump.&quot; You're saying the best thing about Dual-Kith is what <i>I hated the most about it</i> in 1e; that it quickly turned into a Merit everyone takes. There are plenty of useful Merits that over time everyone will probably take when they've got some XP sitting around, and after they're maxed out in their main things.<br /> <br /> One of the big problems is that there are so many Kiths. There's generally multiple Kiths that will orient towards a specific activity. If I want to make a grapple focused Changeling, making a Brollachan, making a Sandharrowed, and making a Dual-Kith Brollochan-Sandharrowed should be equal options. The Dual-Kith one shouldn't be the explicitly best option (as was frequently the case in 1e)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T21:53:34-08:00","id":827308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827293#post827293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is, essentially, your third point. You don't have to miss anything. Custom Kiths are entirely meant to be a thing, and adjusting existing Kiths to suit what your concept is, is already a thing.<br /> <br /> Basically, if you were trying to &quot;sell&quot; me on Dual-Kith, you'd be failing completely, because your core argument is, &quot;Dual Kith is how you make new and flavorful characters,&quot; which amounts to, &quot;failing to take Dual-Kith makes your character a chump.&quot; You're saying the best thing about Dual-Kith is what <i>I hated the most about it</i> in 1e; that it quickly turned into a Merit everyone takes. There are plenty of useful Merits that over time everyone will probably take when they've got some XP sitting around, and after they're maxed out in their main things.<br /> <br /> One of the big problems is that there are so many Kiths. There's generally multiple Kiths that will orient towards a specific activity. If I want to make a grapple focused Changeling, making a Brollachan, making a Sandharrowed, and making a Dual-Kith Brollochan-Sandharrowed should be equal options. The Dual-Kith one shouldn't be the explicitly best option (as was frequently the case in 1e)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well then I guess that's where we disagree, because I'm all for customization. If your argument is basically &quot;Well if you give players the option to have more customization they'll take more customization&quot; then I'm sorry because I don't think the argument of &quot;It's popular, so it shouldn't be included&quot; is a valid line of reason. Most people want it because they want their changelings unique. The more Kiths you put in dramatically increases the available pool of options for what your kith was shaped like. Let's say there's 100, now if each of those 100 can have 100 then we have 100<sup>2 </sup>or 10,000 options available to us. If you add another kith, then you have 100<sup>3</sup> or 1,000,000 options. In a game about roleplaying, having each character unique I believe is fairly important. I don't think any two kiths/durances should be exactly the same so adding options to mix and match I find incredibly appealing, because you're not gated into &quot;Well you gotta pick one or the other&quot; or relying on homebrew which is rather dodgy even when done right. If you want to say &quot;Well everyone's just going to take it&quot; then maybe the game should just offer multiple kiths out of the gate, and compensate players who choose to forego that option with bonus experiences or something to that effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","user":"ReshyShira","date":". 02-10-2016, 01:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T22:16:49-08:00","id":827318,"title":"","content":"Something I don't understand is why multi-kith would be required for making their changelings unique though when you can already mix and reflavour them based on the Kith preview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T22:20:56-08:00","id":827322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827318#post827318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I don't understand is why multi-kith would be required for making their changelings unique though when you can already mix and reflavour them based on the Kith preview.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never said required. Some people think it's required because it's so popular, but that really speaks to me that it's both popular and appealing and that's not a bad thing. I don't thinking having it as an option hurts the game, and frankly if it's so damn popular that everyone uses it then maybe that should be the default is allowing a mix of maybe 2-3 kiths? Those who select less than that could be compensated in bonus experiences.<br /> <br /> At least, that's how I view it. I mean sure you can reflavor them, but it's still expected to resemble the original kith's purpose in some way, and not be a cut and paste of another entirely different kith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T23:24:14-08:00","id":827337,"title":"","content":"Dual Kith primarily exists as shorthanding crunch and compounding crunch.<br /> <br /> As a shorthand, it's when the idea for a kith would take too much mechanical screwery to make a truly unique Kith Blessing for the purposes of the game. If the idea of the character goes beyond reskinning but for some reason can't warrant a new kith with it's own blessing, a Dual Kith works. Or really, if you just don't want to bother-some people just want to work with what's there and clunk it together regardless of the cost.<br /> <br /> As a compound, it's when the character idea benefits from the synergy or asynchronicity of the two kiths, predominantly in a mechanical way. basically, when helps to have to two seperate beneifts that workon their own but create interesting results in play when bounced off or joined together, even if it's only conceptual play.<br /> <br /> As for it's price, I think the right price'd be about 3 Dots. Bit of an expenditure so as to not just be a round-out choice, particularly some of the other excellent merits in the book, but it's also not so expensive as to be nuts.<br /> <br /> I could see a case for 4 though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T00:45:45-08:00","id":827348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827337#post827337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dual Kith primarily exists as shorthanding crunch and compounding crunch.<br /> <br /> As a shorthand, it's when the idea for a kith would take too much mechanical screwery to make a truly unique Kith Blessing for the purposes of the game. If the idea of the character goes beyond reskinning but for some reason can't warrant a new kith with it's own blessing, a Dual Kith works. Or really, if you just don't want to bother-some people just want to work with what's there and clunk it together regardless of the cost.<br /> <br /> As a compound, it's when the character idea benefits from the synergy or asynchronicity of the two kiths, predominantly in a mechanical way. basically, when helps to have to two seperate beneifts that workon their own but create interesting results in play when bounced off or joined together, even if it's only conceptual play.<br /> <br /> As for it's price, I think the right price'd be about 3 Dots. Bit of an expenditure so as to not just be a round-out choice, particularly some of the other excellent merits in the book, but it's also not so expensive as to be nuts.<br /> <br /> I could see a case for 4 though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, a lot of the Kiths focus on doing one thing, and it seems to me that having multiple roles might allow for more interesting options. Doesn't seem to make a whole lot of sense (Though this is the true fae) to give one Changeling access to analyze the wheels and then have to communicate to another one to actually grease the wheels.<br /> <br /> One off the top of my head is based off a book I read where the &quot;utopia&quot; is maintained by terrifying psychic dragons that constantly look for deviant thoughts to drive out. So, in this case you might want to have something to the effect of Draconic + Grey + Oni. Sense the deviant thoughts, locate the deviant in a crowd, intimidate or kill the deviant. A sort of terrifying secret police. Kiths only seem to go over one strict role, so if you were given more than one role (or a highly complex role) than you likely have more than one kith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","user":"ReshyShira","date":". 02-10-2016, 03:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T01:15:12-08:00","id":827352,"title":"","content":"Though I can see the appeal of having two kiths, I honestly can't say it's required - yes, the character I mentioned earlier is one I'd <i>like</i> to have two Kiths for, but I am already making characters who would do fine with just one. In particular I have a Beast Witchtooth who looks like a black cat and doesn't really fit for me to have any kith aside from Witchtooth, even if he's someone who uses his powers to help charm others into pleasant situations that would normally be extremely unlikely for his unpleasant looking mask. Even if multiple kiths are mechanically strategic and popular to take, it doesn't mean that it's not advantageous to spend those merit points elsewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T02:14:54-08:00","id":827362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827308#post827308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well then I guess that's where we disagree, because I'm all for customization.</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, that's missing the point so hard I'm not sure if I should be insulted. You're consistently putting words in my mouth that I'm not saying.<br /> <br /> I'm all for customization to. I love things like separating Kith and Seeming because it allows a ton more customization. I love the book flat out saying to tweak Kiths and not feel bound to the list as presented.<br /> <br /> The problem with Dual-Kith, is that it isn't really about customizing a Kith so that it's perfect for your concept. It's about making a Kith with more powers than other Kiths. That's what it does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If your argument is basically &quot;Well if you give players the option to have more customization they'll take more customization&quot; then I'm sorry because I don't think the argument of &quot;It's popular, so it shouldn't be included&quot; is a valid line of reason. </div> </div> </div>Well, it's not my argument. My argument is what I already posted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most people want it because they want their changelings unique. </div> </div> </div>Which is a problem. There's going to be ~100 Kiths, which isn't an exhaustive list, or a list with no room for non-Merit/other point based customization. With six Seemings, and 100 Kiths, there's already 600 options to get unique with. If that's not enough options to have a unique feeling character (combined with Courts, Contracts, and everything else on their sheet), the problem is not solved by adding Dual-Kiths. Dual-Kiths for this reason is not catering to customization. It's catering to special snowflakes and optimization.<br /> <br /> People manage just fine in lots of other CofD games without a Dual-Splat Merit. VtR don't need a Dual-Clan Merit for players to feel like they're making unique characters. WtF doesn't need Dual-Tribe, or Dual-Auspice. Etc. If people can make unique characters in those games without an equivalent Merit... so can Changeling players. Even Terrible Form doesn't feel the need to mix splats. And the 2e core books so far have been full of customization Merits. There's just general ones like Terrible Form for Demon, or Favored Form for Werewolf, where you pick something your character gets better at in a fashion you want by building on what they already have. CtL 1e had a ton of these sorts of Merits in Rites of Spring as well.<br /> <br /> Even playing with a group of 20 people, 600 options is plenty to avoid overlap; even with a Freehold full of Changelings. You don't need 60,000.<br /> <br /> Dual-Kith to achieve &quot;true&quot; uniqueness is a massive flaw in design. A character should be unique, and then the mechanics should be there to portray the character. If single Kith is not pulling the weight it is supposed to in that regard, than more Kiths per character isn't the solution; figuring out how to make single Kiths do their job is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Some people think it's required because it's so popular, but that really speaks to me that it's both popular and appealing and that's not a bad thing. </div> </div> </div>You're completely missing a major point here Some people think it's required because in 1e (and none of the spoiled 2e mechanics seem to change this) a Dual Kith character could so easily outstrip a single Kith character in the same area of specialization, that it was required to actually make an effective character.<br /> <br /> This isn't about customization, but optimization, and the synergy issues the original Merit created. <br /> <br /> The problem is not that something is popular because it is cool or fun and a lot of people take it. The problem is when something is &quot;popular&quot; because it has become a One True Build. Dual Kith definitely became this in 1e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827337#post827337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for it's price, I think the right price'd be about 3 Dots. Bit of an expenditure so as to not just be a round-out choice, particularly some of the other excellent merits in the book, but it's also not so expensive as to be nuts.<br /> <br /> I could see a case for 4 though.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's pretty hard for those of us not involved in writing the book directly to say. :P<br /> <br /> If CtL 2e Core manages to provide a Merit list that really puts Dual Kith in a pile of equally awesome Merits for the price in a way that RoS completely failed to do? I'd be satisfied. Hell, house-ruling a non-scaling Merit's cost is pretty much the easiest thing to house rule if I disagree with the final cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T02:20:44-08:00","id":827364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827348#post827348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, a lot of the Kiths focus on doing one thing, and it seems to me that having multiple roles might allow for more interesting options. Doesn't seem to make a whole lot of sense (Though this is the true fae) to give one Changeling access to analyze the wheels and then have to communicate to another one to actually grease the wheels.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's not really any reason that the entirety of a Fae's workings stick when the entire point of a Seeming is to break the Fae's workings, and then you leave Arcadia and end up back on Earth, which doesn't play by Arcadian rules.<br /> <br /> I mean, what you describe would be kinda ironic, which we've totally absolutely positively established counts as cold iron, yeah? (I'm being wishfully sarcastic; it has not really been indisputably confirmed to my knowledge. (Also, I hate that I have to explain that.)) <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827348#post827348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One off the top of my head is based off a book I read where the &quot;utopia&quot; is maintained by terrifying psychic dragons that constantly look for deviant thoughts to drive out. So, in this case you might want to have something to the effect of Draconic + Grey + Oni. Sense the deviant thoughts, locate the deviant in a crowd, intimidate or kill the deviant. A sort of terrifying secret police. Kiths only seem to go over one strict role, so if you were given more than one role (or a highly complex role) than you likely have more than one kith.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm curious how many Merit dots you'd be willing to spend on a triple-Blessing like that. Four? Six? Eight? At character creation, or after? Like... how much is the concept worth to you, or would you actually compromise on how it's expressed mechanically when you're at the table?<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd still try to distill the essence of what I wanted from being a psychic dragon secret policeman into a single Blessing and just use fluff for the rest. But I don't particularly want to play that concept, so it's hard for me to actually come up with a suitable Blessing.<br /> <br /> I think everyone on the thread agrees that having the option is a good option to have as a general principle. I don't see the point, but I'm not going to stop you or anything as long as you pay for any mechanical benefit you get with proportionate point-buy. (Or we require everyone to pick 2+ Kiths. That works for me, too. Personally, the homebrew I'd consider is getting rid of Kith Blessings altogether, but I think most people would be sad about losing their freebies.)</span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T10:11:07-08:00","id":827598,"title":"","content":"I think if you're really bothered by some character building choices bring sub-optimal, CofD is not going to be the system for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T11:00:16-08:00","id":827623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827362#post827362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, that's missing the point so hard I'm not sure if I should be insulted. You're consistently putting words in my mouth that I'm not saying.<br /> <br /> I'm all for customization to. I love things like separating Kith and Seeming because it allows a ton more customization. I love the book flat out saying to tweak Kiths and not feel bound to the list as presented.<br /> <br /> The problem with Dual-Kith, is that it isn't really about customizing a Kith so that it's perfect for your concept. It's about making a Kith with more powers than other Kiths. That's what it does.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can technically tweak anything, and you probably will. What's preventing you from &quot;tweaking&quot; a kith to have more powers than it already does? Certain Kiths already have more powers or utility than others. I don't see &quot;Well this kith has one less ability, so it sucks and no one will ever use it.&quot; as a good line of reasoning. I'm not of the option that all kiths were created equal.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827362#post827362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is a problem. There's going to be ~100 Kiths, which isn't an exhaustive list, or a list with no room for non-Merit/other point based customization. With six Seemings, and 100 Kiths, there's already 600 options to get unique with. If that's not enough options to have a unique feeling character (combined with Courts, Contracts, and everything else on their sheet), the problem is not solved by adding Dual-Kiths. Dual-Kiths for this reason is not catering to customization. It's catering to special snowflakes and optimization.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I am sorry if you find the idea of mixing changeling kiths devalues the validity of the experience for you. You're complaining of it from an optimization standpoint, which, frankly, is not really valid here I wouldn't say. It's a roleplaying game, not a competitive multiplayer experience. Were this a video game I could see that line of reasoning having some validity, but this isn't that environment.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827362#post827362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People manage just fine in lots of other CofD games without a Dual-Splat Merit. VtR don't need a Dual-Clan Merit for players to feel like they're making unique characters. WtF doesn't need Dual-Tribe, or Dual-Auspice. Etc. If people can make unique characters in those games without an equivalent Merit... so can Changeling players. Even Terrible Form doesn't feel the need to mix splats. And the 2e core books so far have been full of customization Merits. There's just general ones like Terrible Form for Demon, or Favored Form for Werewolf, where you pick something your character gets better at in a fashion you want by building on what they already have. CtL 1e had a ton of these sorts of Merits in Rites of Spring as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, what are you talking about? Kiths and Form Mods are almost identical. Both are a representation of the function(s) you served while in the service of the Gentry/God-Machine. Heck, many of the flavored texts for the form abilities are strikingly similar to those of changeling descriptions. Kiths aren't about your clan/tribe/agenda/etc. They're about what function you served for the Gentry, they have no (or very little) impact on your Seeming, Court, Entitlements, etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827362#post827362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even playing with a group of 20 people, 600 options is plenty to avoid overlap; even with a Freehold full of Changelings. You don't need 60,000.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay that's your opinion, and my opinion is that I'd rather more options rather than less.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827362#post827362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dual-Kith to achieve &quot;true&quot; uniqueness is a massive flaw in design. A character should be unique, and then the mechanics should be there to portray the character. If single Kith is not pulling the weight it is supposed to in that regard, than more Kiths per character isn't the solution; figuring out how to make single Kiths do their job is.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I wonder if you're under the assumption that a player can't find more than a single kith would fit their character's durance. Kiths also cannot possibly cover every single iteration of every single concept ever made ever, that's hardly possible. However, being able to mix them easily adds to the amount that the Kiths can cover. Not everyone's going to find one single kith fits the durance of the character. If you can, then that's great, but not everyone will and they shouldn't be expected to pander to your specific needs. If you're running a changeling game, feel free to ban dual-kiths. That's your prerogative as a ST.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827362#post827362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're completely missing a major point here Some people think it's required because in 1e (and none of the spoiled 2e mechanics seem to change this) a Dual Kith character could so easily outstrip a single Kith character in the same area of specialization, that it was required to actually make an effective character.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Some people&quot; say lots of things. That's not a compelling line of reasoning. If your concern is being outshined because someone has a second Kith, then that's a little more valid of a concern. However, that can easily be resolved without having to enforce banning a merit over the entire game.<br /> <br /> Plus, in the end, if both of you are specialized in the same things and are having conflicts... I don't think the presence or lack of a kith will solve any problems.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827362#post827362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't about customization, but optimization, and the synergy issues the original Merit created.<br /> <br /> The problem is not that something is popular because it is cool or fun and a lot of people take it. The problem is when something is &quot;popular&quot; because it has become a One True Build. Dual Kith definitely became this in 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like I'm on the Dungeons &amp; Dragons board. Did I made a wrong turn somewhere?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827364#post827364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's not really any reason that the entirety of a Fae's workings stick when the entire point of a Seeming is to break the Fae's workings, and then you leave Arcadia and end up back on Earth, which doesn't play by Arcadian rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the Kiths are the leftovers of the powers you had (Not unlike how Demons work). I mean if you want to play it that way then no Kiths should have any blessings associated with it because they broke it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827364#post827364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious how many Merit dots you'd be willing to spend on a triple-Blessing like that. Four? Six? Eight? At character creation, or after? Like... how much is the concept worth to you, or would you actually compromise on how it's expressed mechanically when you're at the table?</div> </div> </div> </div>Something less than 10 at char gen. The way Kiths work, it seems like something you'd start with, since Kiths are a reflection of your durance in some manner. Gaining some later on I think would be a little odd, I'd think.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827364#post827364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'd still try to distill the essence of what I wanted from being a psychic dragon secret policeman into a single Blessing and just use fluff for the rest. But I don't particularly want to play that concept, so it's hard for me to actually come up with a suitable Blessing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Homebrewing Kiths relies on you having a permissible ST, and as far as I know there's no real rules for making your own, which makes it extremely dodgy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827364#post827364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think everyone on the thread agrees that having the option is a good option to have as a general principle. I don't see the point, but I'm not going to stop you or anything as long as you pay for any mechanical benefit you get with proportionate point-buy. (Or we require everyone to pick 2+ Kiths. That works for me, too. Personally, the homebrew I'd consider is getting rid of Kith Blessings altogether, but I think most people would be sad about losing their freebies.)[/FONT]</div> </div> </div> </div>The point of having dual-kiths is two fold. One is to present it as a valid way to play, second is to show how much the ability is &quot;worth&quot; in game terms. If it's super popular, like everyone keeps saying, then I don't see why offering that as the default option is a bad idea.<br /> <br /> If you want to strip blessings away altogether than that's fine, it'd certainly solve any issues of mixing kiths being &quot;optimal&quot; and not being &quot;sub-optimal&quot; though it may be a bit of a heavy handed way to go about it.<br /> <br /> I will say though, being able to demonstrate an ability rather than saying you possess it is fairly important in a &quot;show don't tell&quot; sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T12:38:52-08:00","id":827706,"title":"","content":"The preview document states really clearly and explicitly that you're allowed to create custom kiths, and if you're not comfortable coming up with something from scratch it gives clear examples of how to mix and match abilities and flavor from the existing list.<br /> <br /> I'm in favor of Dual Kith as a merit, but I have to admit it's because I like playing around with synergies, not because I have difficulty matching concepts to existing mechanics.<br /> <br /> The utility varies kith to kith, but 3 dots sounds cheap to me, given that several kiths include attribute increases in their blessing. I could spend 4 experience to raise my stamina... or I could spend 3 on one of the kiths that does that *and* pick up another cool trick or two. It winds up being heavily mechanically incentivized, which makes it less of an interesting choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T15:12:08-08:00","id":827818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827598#post827598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think if you're really bothered by some character building choices bring sub-optimal, CofD is not going to be the system for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's a false dichotomy. We're allow to dislike extremes of optimization issues, and be OK with a smaller subjective acceptable range of optimization levels.<br /> <br /> I can say, &quot;this is too big of a difference between optimal and sub-optimal that it needs addressing,&quot; without having to avoid a system that I might love for dozens of other reasons because there is some possible optimization gap.<br /> <br /> I also find this kind of silly when a number of the changes CofD made mechanically actually addressed optimization issues in 1e (even if that wasn't the only reason for doing so); such as dumping the over-powered multi-attack Merits, linear XP costs, and making trading Merit dots for Power Stat dots no longer disparate in value.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827623#post827623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can technically tweak anything, and you probably will.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. And I don't need to force players to spend XP/Merit dots to do it either. If my group feels a Kith is weak or a bit too powerful - even in the context of a specific game instance that might not be true in other circumstances - we'll just talk about it and tweak things to make the game more fun. Not charge one PC more, or give another more stuff to make up for it.<br /> <br /> There's no way to make all Kiths objectively equally useful, because the books can't actually predict what specific stuff a group will run. A combat heavy game is going to make certain Kiths more valuable, that would be less value in a social/politics oriented game. The best the books can do is try to make the Kiths good for what they are designed to do in a way that feels roughly equal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, I am sorry if you find the idea of mixing changeling kiths devalues the validity of the experience for you. </div> </div> </div>Did I say that? No. <b>Stop claiming I'm saying things I did not <i>fucking</i> say</b>.<br /> <br /> In the passage you cited, I said that 600 options along just two axes of character traits is plenty for addressing the desire for characters to be unique. Nothing in there says, &quot;I find the idea of mixing changeling Kiths devalues the experience,&quot; I said that Dual Kiths a bad way to ensure the opportunity to make your character feels unique.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're complaining of it from an optimization standpoint, which, frankly, is not really valid here I wouldn't say. </div> </div> </div>Sorry. No. You don't get to declare validity here. It's a game. The game side of things has to work; which includes things like the rules producing desired results. One True Builds are not desired results in CtL.<br /> <br /> You also don't get to dictate what's a &quot;right way&quot; to play the game. I've been in a fairly PvP competitive CtL chat-based game with a lot of political scheming. It was lots of fun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Uh, what are you talking about? </div> </div> </div>None of the other CofD games needing &quot;Dual-Kith&quot; equivalents to make unique characters.<br /> <br /> Are you actually reading, or just responding to random nonsense and imagining I said it? Because I was pretty clear when I said, &quot;People manage just fine in lots of other CofD games without a Dual-Splat Merit.&quot; as on opening line to that paragraph.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Okay that's your opinion, and my opinion is that I'd rather more options rather than less. </div> </div> </div>You have infinite options in the ability to make custom Kiths.<br /> <br /> As well, from a non-purely-subjective design standpoint too many options is, in fact, a problem. Too many options leads to decision paralysis where players are overwhelmed by the number of choices. Hell, in one of the other open dev threads it was acknowledged that the large number of Kiths already in the book need to be presented properly to help players quickly find Kiths that match their concepts instead of having to sort through the full list.<br /> <br /> Consider, for a moment, what 60,000 options for one choice means. If you average 30 sec of consideration per option, it will take almost 3 weeks straight (no sleep, no breaks, all the time just reading your options and weighing them to make your decision) to consider them all.<br /> <br /> That's insane for a game. That's why games generally use multiple axis splat design instead. Two decisions with five options each (10 considerations) is distinctly faster than one decision of 25 options (25 considerations) even if they result in the same number of combinations.<br /> <br /> I'm not playing Changeling because I want to spend a month to figure out what Kith/Dual Kith combination is the best fit for my idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You know, I wonder if you're under the assumption that a player can't find more than a single kith would fit their character's durance. </div> </div> </div>Yay. Another bullshit strawman.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Kiths also cannot possibly cover every single iteration of every single concept ever made ever, that's hardly possible. </div> </div> </div>And Dual Kiths <b>does not change this</b>.<br /> <br /> That's why we use abstraction in RPGs. No Skill list can ever possibly cover every single iteration of every single field of scientific inquiry ever made ever. That's why we just lump it all together and call it Science. Yes, we have Specialties and Merits to differentiate difference characters with Science, but you don't have to take Dual-Major to make a biochemist.<br /> <br /> Dual Kith is valuable when it fills the exact role of being an <i>option</i> to cover edge cases. It doesn't work when it exists to be one of the default way of expanding options.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If your concern is being outshined because someone has a second Kith, then that's a little more valid of a concern. </div> </div> </div>This is not an abstract concern. Though I'm not concerned about being outshined (I ST more than I play), and in fact the biggest blow up that happened to me because of this was because I was outshining the crap out of two other characters to the point where we had to restart play because their players were just sitting there doing nothing because mine hand it handled before they could do anything. I agreed, because I'm not that big of an ass, and I wasn't trying to do that. But that definitely informed my opinions on the 1e iteration of the Merit.<br /> <br /> I'm concerned, as an experienced player, that I'll make the game unfun because I'm way more used to taking advantages of synergies than newer players and they'll not get engaged with the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, that can easily be resolved without having to enforce banning a merit over the entire game. </div> </div> </div>Maybe.<br /> <br /> Also, please cite me once saying I want to ban the Merit from the game. Otherwise, again, stop claiming I'm saying things I didn't say.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel like I'm on the Dungeons &amp; Dragons board. Did I made a wrong turn somewhere? </div> </div> </div>Apparently when you left the, &quot;Role-players not Roll-players,&quot; corner of the Internet and decided that kind of BS would fly with a general audience.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Homebrewing Kiths relies on you having a permissible ST, and as far as I know there's no real rules for making your own, which makes it extremely dodgy. </div> </div> </div>Ah... the hypocrisy of it. You realize that to me, you're basically arguing, &quot;screw the details of the rules, I want to make my concept!&quot; and then going, &quot;But there aren't rules for it so you can't count on doing it.&quot;<br /> <br /> The only real rule we've seen is the most important one: STs should be permissible about allowing customized Kiths.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The point of having dual-kiths is two fold. One is to present it as a valid way to play, second is to show how much the ability is &quot;worth&quot; in game terms. If it's super popular, like everyone keeps saying, then I don't see why offering that as the default option is a bad idea. </div> </div> </div>Oddly not what someone involved in writing CtL 2e said...<br /> <br /> Also, the 1e implementation significantly failed at part 2. Lots of the Kith Blessings in 1e could be replicated with other Merits. The issue was those Merits ranged significantly in value. Dual Kith resulted in being cheaper than some some Kith Blessings were worth if replicated with Merits, or more expensive than others.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T15:25:49-08:00","id":827826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827818#post827818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's a false dichotomy. We're allow to dislike extremes of optimization issues, and be OK with a smaller subjective acceptable range of optimization levels.<br /> <br /> I can say, &amp;quot;this is too big of a difference between optimal and sub-optimal that it needs addressing,&amp;quot; without having to avoid a system that I might love for dozens of other reasons because there is some possible optimization gap.<br /> <br /> I also find this kind of silly when a number of the changes CofD made mechanically actually addressed optimization issues in 1e (even if that wasn't the only reason for doing so); such as dumping the over-powered multi-attack Merits, linear XP costs, and making trading Merit dots for Power Stat dots no longer disparate in value.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair. I guess we just have different thresholds for that sort of thing. That, and I don't see taking two of the kith blessings we've seen so far as being a strictly better choice than taking one Blessing and 3 or 4 dots of Merits. YMMV.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T16:10:03-08:00","id":827843,"title":"","content":"Gargantuan gives you a dot of presence (4XP), 4 dots of Heavy Weapons (4XP, albeit a modified version) and the ability to grow in size. That's the most extreme example I saw, but it's definitely not the only one where there's a pretty clear &quot;right&quot; choice from an XP metric whether you go dual kith or try to match the abilities with other merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T16:25:57-08:00","id":827848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827362#post827362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People manage just fine in lots of other CofD games without a Dual-Splat Merit. VtR don't need a Dual-Clan Merit for players to feel like they're making unique characters. WtF doesn't need Dual-Tribe, or Dual-Auspice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to undermine the rest of your post that I basically agree with, but <i>come on</i>.<br /> <br /> DUAL CLAN MERIT WOULD BE SICK","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T16:29:09-08:00","id":827849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827843#post827843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gargantuan gives you a dot of presence (4XP), 4 dots of Heavy Weapons (4XP, albeit a modified version) and the ability to grow in size. That's the most extreme example I saw, but it's definitely not the only one where there's a pretty clear &quot;right&quot; choice from an XP metric whether you go dual kith or try to match the abilities with other merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, if you're trying to reproduce the exact effect of a Kith, Dual-Kith is going to be the most efficient way to do it. In other news, if you want to reproduce the exact effect of Professional Training, Professional Training is the most efficient way to do it, and water is wet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T16:38:03-08:00","id":827852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">I think if you're really bothered by some character building choices bring sub-optimal, CofD is not going to be the system for you.</span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel like I'm on the Dungeons &amp; Dragons board. Did I made a wrong turn somewhere? </div> </div> </div>I think these are horrible attitudes to have. Especially when the issue being discussed isn't that something is sub-optimal, but that it Was too optimal... It seems like whenever someone ever has a valid concern about balance of something everyone immediately goes &quot;Who cares&quot; or &quot;This system is wrong for you&quot; despite the fact that Large disparities in power or One-True-Builds can harm peoples roleplaying and enjoyment. Simply being a roleplaying game does not make the concern invalid. One of the primary reasons we even have RPG's is so we have a rules framework for fair roleplaying rather than just freeform playing pretend It doesn't enhance the unique-ness of characters if one of the primary reasons it's being taken is because it's an obvious choice mechanically. If something is obviously the more powerful option and is poorly assigned it's cost, that's an issue. And if such a thing could reasonable be fixed, then it's lazy to simply ignore it and not try to mitigate that issue simply because you think the ruleset you have designed is above the concept of balance.<br /> <br /> Also the number of people on this board who seem to use D&amp;D as a pejorative is ridiculous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T16:51:54-08:00","id":827858,"title":"","content":"I said match, not replicate, and that word choice was deliberate. 8+ experience worth of dots for 3 invested is an incredibly good deal. You don't have to be trying to reproduce the exact effect to run into issues where a Dual Kith is just better at a party role because they got more return for their dots. Not every choice needs to be equally viable, but the more discrepancy there is the more likely you are to have problems with one character feeling useless next to another, and that isn't fun for the players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T16:57:48-08:00","id":827859,"title":"","content":"I don't actually have any problem with character optimization. In fact, I'm a big optimizer myself, especially in D&amp;D, which I love. That said, if you are really bothered by some choices being more exp efficient than others, you are going to have a rough time with CofD because there are many such choices in the game. That's not a value judgment, it's an observation. Just look at the afformentioned Professional Training, or Mystery Cult Initiation. The physical disciplines in Vampire are strictly better than buying up Attributes and they cost the same amount of experience out-of-clan, less in-clan. Heck, Striking Looks is just a Skill specialty with Interdisciplinary Specialty (and Area of Expertise if you take the 2 dot version) for 1 exp cheaper. These kinds of optimally efficient and inefficient choices are all over CofD, in no small part because the majority of the developers subscribe to the &quot;balance is an illusion&quot; philosophy. YMMV on if that's a problem, how severe of a problem it is, or whether it spoils your enjoyment of the rest of the game. I'm not saying &quot;if you don't like it, get out&quot;, I'm saying if you're arguing from a place of designing based around curtailing char op, you're not going to make much headway given CofD's design philosophy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-10-2016, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T17:22:19-08:00","id":827875,"title":"","content":"I've been getting into CoD/Changeling because it doesn't trigger my min-maxing instincts as harshly as many games. I suppose that's because I can't assume the ability to pour on points of damage is going to be a reliable fallback solution. Since it's a horror game, people are probably more willing to write down a monster's combat stats as &quot;<a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/HaHaHaNo\" target=\"_blank\">Ha, ha, no</a>. <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/RunOrDie\" target=\"_blank\">Run. Just Run</a>.&quot; Lot of things a Motley needs to potentially cover, and different Storytellers and scenes require different skills among a team's pool. I think that ends up meaning that a Storyteller probably shouldn't worry so much about the min-maxer always outshining the creative guy who doesn't know the rules as well.<br /> <br /> If someone wants to do cool stuff in my Chronicle, I've got a general rule I've decided on: If you've got 4+ dots in a skill, especially if it's enhanced by merits, feel free to sprinkle in a little supernatural flair to how you describe your actions when using that skill. I figure it's another way to express the benefits of their Durance that might not fit into a Kith, and it's hopefully a way to make something as &quot;boring&quot; as skills more interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T18:09:41-08:00","id":827896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827859#post827859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't actually have any problem with character optimization. In fact, I'm a big optimizer myself, especially in D&amp;D, which I love. That said, if you are really bothered by some choices being more exp efficient than others, you are going to have a rough time with CofD because there are many such choices in the game. That's not a value judgment, it's an observation. Just look at the afformentioned Professional Training, or Mystery Cult Initiation. The physical disciplines in Vampire are strictly better than buying up Attributes and they cost the same amount of experience out-of-clan, less in-clan. Heck, Striking Looks is just a Skill specialty with Interdisciplinary Specialty (and Area of Expertise if you take the 2 dot version) for 1 exp cheaper. These kinds of optimally efficient and inefficient choices are all over CofD, in no small part because the majority of the developers subscribe to the &quot;balance is an illusion&quot; philosophy. YMMV on if that's a problem, how severe of a problem it is, or whether it spoils your enjoyment of the rest of the game. I'm not saying &quot;if you don't like it, get out&quot;, I'm saying if you're arguing from a place of designing based around curtailing char op, you're not going to make much headway given CofD's design philosophy.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Balance is an illusion&quot; isn't a bad idea, but it shouldn't be used as a way to wave away all balance concerns. The basic idea, that perfect balance isn't even something you should try to achieve, is sound. The problem is that you do actually have to take the time to maintain the illusion. Options that are obviously better (and Professional Training is one of those, but the theory that it's only intended for mortal characters has always made a lot of sense to me) aren't a great idea on principle. They cause the illusion to break down, and any player with the slightest mechanistic bent will gravitate towards them and eschew other options. Not the worst thing in the world, but it may lead to a situation where you invalidate text written elsewhere.<br /> <br /> Where it gets really bad is when some members of the group are interested in creating strong characters with powerful internal synergies, while others don't care about reading the mechanics so closely. If your system naturally leads to a situation where mixed groups of players include some who are clearly and evidently outclassed, there's a very good chance of a negative play experience and a negative impact on the game. The illusion is important. Strict balance isn't necessary, but the perception of balance is vital.<br /> <br /> It's yet to be seen whether Dual-Kith is one of those &quot;obviously better&quot; abilities, but it was in first edition so I sympathise with Heavy Arms' concern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T18:33:57-08:00","id":827904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827623#post827623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Homebrewing Kiths relies on you having a permissible ST, and as far as I know there's no real rules for making your own, which makes it extremely dodgy.</div> </div> </div> </div>FYI, <i>all</i> Merit selection requires having a permissible ST. Making it a Merit doesn't solve this problem at all.<br /> <br /> And this gets back to my entire problem of the &quot;our STs are horrible people who won't let us play with any thing except the strictest, most literal reading of the rules in ways that are carefully designed to minimize our fun&quot; argument. If you have, or are, an ST like this? It's not worth playing the game. Find something else to do with your time, or get another ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T18:44:12-08:00","id":827910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827826#post827826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's fair. I guess we just have different thresholds for that sort of thing. That, and I don't see taking two of the kith blessings we've seen so far as being a strictly better choice than taking one Blessing and 3 or 4 dots of Merits. YMMV.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's worth restating that my position isn't set for 2e, because we haven't seen the final drafts of anything yet. If 2e's Merit section puts Rites of Spring's Merit section to the shame it wholly deserves? Wonderful! Dual Kith can do it's job as weird edge case mixed Kiths with some mechanical buffs, but I'll have lots of awesome Merits besides it to make my PCs awesome at stuff via their one Kith when that's appropriate.<br /> <br /> I largely trust that the 2e authors have a good eye for this, because there's a lot less problematic Merits so far, despite there being a ton of awesome ones that are actually some serious headscratchers to pick between when you're low on XP. And with only a small number of ones that have problems like this are identified, it's pretty easy to deal with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T18:54:28-08:00","id":827915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827896#post827896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Balance is an illusion&quot; isn't a bad idea, but it shouldn't be used as a way to wave away all balance concerns. The basic idea, that perfect balance isn't even something you should try to achieve, is sound. The problem is that you do actually have to take the time to maintain the illusion. Options that are obviously better (and Professional Training is one of those, but the theory that it's only intended for mortal characters has always made a lot of sense to me) aren't a great idea on principle. They cause the illusion to break down, and any player with the slightest mechanistic bent will gravitate towards them and eschew other options. Not the worst thing in the world, but it may lead to a situation where you invalidate text written elsewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not trying to use &quot;balance is an illusion&quot; to excuse anything, I'm just pointing out that your desire not to have obviously more exp efficient choices is demonstrably not a concern for the developers. The fact that Professional Training is in the general Merits section and doesn't have mortal as a prerequisite is proof that it's not only intended for mortal characters. The fact that it exists at all is proof that the developers are cool with some Merits giving characters more bang for their buck. I'm not unsympathetic to the concern that Dual Kith might end up being a Merit tax for some groups, but the evidence would seem to indicate that the developers tend to let groups sort out those issues for themselves, rather than letting the potential for those issues constrain their design.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827896#post827896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where it gets really bad is when some members of the group are interested in creating strong characters with powerful internal synergies, while others don't care about reading the mechanics so closely. If your system naturally leads to a situation where mixed groups of players include some who are clearly and evidently outclassed, there's a very good chance of a negative play experience and a negative impact on the game. The illusion is important. Strict balance isn't necessary, but the perception of balance is vital.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds to me like a problem that would be better solved by a solid session 0 and open dialogue with your group than by trying to design around it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827896#post827896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's yet to be seen whether Dual-Kith is one of those &quot;obviously better&quot; abilities, but it was in first edition so I sympathise with Heavy Arms' concern.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can understand that. I found Dual Kith to be a huge problem in 1e for similar reasons, although in my case the problem was more that it was essential to so many character concepts than anything to do with &quot;balance&quot;. It was a tax because you basically had to take it if you wanted to play a character with animal features but didn't want to be Beast Seeming (or whatever), not because it let people get too many bonuses. In 2e, I don't see the same issue coming up because Kith is no longer tied to Seeming. Sure, with the newly powered-up Kith Blessings it will be a powerful Merit, which may lead a lot of characters to take it. But since taking it will mean missing out on the [redacted] Fighting Style, or a few dots of Hollow, or an extra dot of Wyrd at character creation, I don't see it becoming a tax. Not all character concepts (or all char op builds, if that's more your thing) are going to benefit from a second Kith Blessing over other options they could take. That's where the &quot;other options will be suboptimal&quot; argument falls flat for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-10-2016, 10:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T18:59:44-08:00","id":827918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827910#post827910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's worth restating that my position isn't set for 2e, because we haven't seen the final drafts of anything yet. If 2e's Merit section puts Rites of Spring's Merit section to the shame it wholly deserves? Wonderful! Dual Kith can do it's job as weird edge case mixed Kiths with some mechanical buffs, but I'll have lots of awesome Merits besides it to make my PCs awesome at stuff via their one Kith when that's appropriate.<br /> <br /> I largely trust that the 2e authors have a good eye for this, because there's a lot less problematic Merits so far, despite there being a ton of awesome ones that are actually some serious headscratchers to pick between when you're low on XP. And with only a small number of ones that have problems like this are identified, it's pretty easy to deal with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense. My perspective might be coming in part from the fact that my playtest character did take Dual Kith, and it was not an easy choice for me. Ultimately I decided that the character concept was better served by taking Dual-Kith than by building a custom Kith and taking some of the other options I was looking at, but as I said, it was a tough call.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-10-2016, 10:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T19:14:46-08:00","id":827924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827904#post827904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">FYI, <i>all</i> Merit selection requires having a permissible ST. Making it a Merit doesn't solve this problem at all.<br /> <br /> And this gets back to my entire problem of the &quot;our STs are horrible people who won't let us play with any thing except the strictest, most literal reading of the rules in ways that are carefully designed to minimize our fun&quot; argument. If you have, or are, an ST like this? It's not worth playing the game. Find something else to do with your time, or get another ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that kind of ignores the whole middle. I know some STs are uncomfortable with allowing anything that's not printed in the rulebooks, while others are happier to adlib or flex the rules quite greatly. I feel it is the whole reason there's whole chapters in books such as Demon and Changeling 1E for homebrewing your own ideas, and the like - because again, some people will need that advice, want that advice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T20:00:17-08:00","id":827938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827924#post827924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel it is the whole reason there's whole chapters in books such as Demon and Changeling 1E for homebrewing your own ideas, and the like - because again, some people will need that advice, want that advice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. I really hope people start realizing that advice should be followed sometimes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T20:02:41-08:00","id":827943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827915#post827915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not trying to use &quot;balance is an illusion&quot; to excuse anything, I'm just pointing out that your desire not to have obviously more exp efficient choices is demonstrably not a concern for the developers. The fact that Professional Training is in the general Merits section and doesn't have mortal as a prerequisite is proof that it's not only intended for mortal characters. The fact that it exists at all is proof that the developers are cool with some Merits giving characters more bang for their buck. I'm not unsympathetic to the concern that Dual Kith might end up being a Merit tax for some groups, but the evidence would seem to indicate that the developers tend to let groups sort out those issues for themselves, rather than letting the potential for those issues constrain their design.</div> </div> </div> </div>Professional Training is also only printed in Demon and the core book, right? And wasn't reprinted in Vampire or Werewolf despite them being self-contained? I'm actually not sure. I just remember reading something to that effect and going, &quot;Oh, yeah, that's not a bad solution&quot;.<br /> <br /> But that's a separate issue. The existence of Professional Training doesn't render that kind of design choice immune to criticism for its potential negative impact on a game, nor does the developer's preference for a style of design mean that they shouldn't listen to feedback from players concerned about that direction. I mean, you're welcome to say that's useless to argue, that it won't charge the minds of any of the developers, or that you can always change things at your own table to suit how you want to play. And all of that is (or may be) accurate, but isn't really a counter-argument to the actual point being made.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827915#post827915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sounds to me like a problem that would be better solved by a solid session 0 and open dialogue with your group than by trying to design around it.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, I can play around anything. I'd just rather that I didn't have to. Beginning every campaign with either &quot;You guys who like tailoring your characters to a fine polish, please tone it down&quot; or &quot;You guys who don't care about the mechanics, please do your homework if you want to compete&quot; isn't an ideal situation. Not if the game could be written to reduce the gap to begin with.<br /> <br /> Thus far, I think Mummy has been the best game for this. Just ignore 1st edition's awful Fighting Style design and there aren't any merits that pose a problem, Affinities vary a bit in quality but those that are bad for a concept are usually obviously useless at the concept stage (i.e. if you don't see a need to jump really far, don't get Falcon Soul Aloft) rather than bad in the implementation of the mechanics, and I think there was only one Utterance in the entire game that didn't really gel mechanically (Waters of Life). That's not to say all powers are equal, but it is very hard to make a Mummy who can't contribute to a party. So it's not an impossible demand by any means.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827915#post827915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can understand that. I found Dual Kith to be a huge problem in 1e for similar reasons, although in my case the problem was more that it had more to do with concept than with &quot;balance&quot;. It was a tax because if you wanted to play a character with animal features but didn't want to be Beast Seeming (or whatever), not because it let people get too many bonuses. In 2e, I don't see the same issue coming up because Kith is no longer tied to Seeming. Sure, with the newly powered-up Kith Blessings it will be a powerful Merit, which may lead a lot of characters to take it. But since taking it will mean missing out on the [redacted] Fighting Style, or a few dots of Haven, or an extra dot of Wyrd at character creation, I don't see it becoming a tax. Not all character concepts (or chat op builds, if that's your style) are going to benefit from a second Kith Blessing over other options they could take. That's where the &quot;other options will be suboptimal&quot; argument falls flat for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Taking the Dual Kith always used to lead to you having fewer dots in Wyrd/Hollow/Fighting Style. And in first edition, Fighting Style was arguably a bigger deal than it is now. However, all those are things you can pick up as the game progresses. Kiths as representation of the Durance may put pressure on mechanically minded players to take it at character creation. Kiths that draw on Wyrd as the basis of their strength become an increasingly stronger investment as the game goes on. Small changes at character creation can lead to impossibly vast differences at the late game, something that is going to be very hard to judge when the possible combinations are as immense as they are.<br /> <br /> None of this is to say Dual Kith is actually going to be bad for this game and shouldn't be included. I'm just taking exception to the idea that balance should not be a serious, even primary, concern in that decision. After all, if you want beast-like attributes without a beast-like Kith/Seeming, just say that you have them or refluff an existing Kith. Not every aesthetic choice needs to be backed by mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T20:13:41-08:00","id":827948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827826#post827826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's fair. I guess we just have different thresholds for that sort of thing. That, and I don't see taking two of the kith blessings we've seen so far as being a strictly better choice than taking one Blessing and 3 or 4 dots of Merits. YMMV.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There are several Kiths that provide benefits that would cost significantly more to buy with xp or that are equivalent to more than 3-4 dots worth of merits. (Like the example HelmsDerp provided.) There are also a couple Kiths which are underwhelming compared to 3-4 dots worth of merits. Dual Kith has the potential of exacerbating this issue when one player uses Dual Kith to take two highly optimal options (possibly made even more optimal through synergy) and another player takes one of the more sub-optimal Kiths. Then the ST is left in the unenviable position of telling one of the two players to modify their character so they can be somewhat more balanced or struggling to make sure the overpowered character doesn't constantly steal the limelight.<br /> <br /> I'm in favor of keeping Dual Kith, personally, but I think it needs to be at least 4 dots and come with a &quot;requires ST approval&quot; caveat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T20:44:25-08:00","id":827959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827943#post827943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Professional Training is also only printed in Demon and the core book, right? And wasn't reprinted in Vampire or Werewolf despite them being self-contained? I'm actually not sure. I just remember reading something to that effect and going, &quot;Oh, yeah, that's not a bad solution&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's correct, but it's not specified as a human only Merit. Restricting it to only human characters is a perfectly reasonable ruling, but so is saying that it's available to anyone. It's presumably at least available to Demons since it's in their core book and not specified as being unavailable to them. But I digress.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827943#post827943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that's a separate issue. The existence of Professional Training doesn't render that kind of design choice immune to criticism for its potential negative impact on a game, nor does the developer's preference for a style of design mean that they shouldn't listen to feedback from players concerned about that direction. I mean, you're welcome to say that's useless to argue, that it won't charge the minds of any of the developers, or that you can always change things at your own table to suit how you want to play. And all of that is (or may be) accurate, but isn't really a counter-argument to the actual point being made.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's not unreasonable to critique. I'm just saying, if these kinds of Merits are a problem for you, it's pretty much a fact of CofD you're going to need to learn to deal with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827943#post827943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, I can play around anything. I'd just rather that I didn't have to. Beginning every campaign with either &quot;You guys who like tailoring your characters to a fine polish, please tone it down&quot; or &quot;You guys who don't care about the mechanics, please do your homework if you want to compete&quot; isn't an ideal situation. Not if the game could be written to reduce the gap to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is, I think, where our philosophies diverge. I don't think it should be the game's job to try to fix the group's problems. It constrains design and it's just generally not very effective, since the game rules can only attempt to deal with such problems preeptively, and they can't possibly anticipate the needs of every group. Better in my opinion to leave the design unconstrained by such concerns and provide solid advice for groups to deal with their own problems. That's a pretty fundamental game design philosophy division though, and I don't expect either of us to be able to change the other's mind, so this might be an agree to disagree kind of thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827943#post827943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thus far, I think Mummy has been the best game for this. Just ignore 1st edition's awful Fighting Style design and there aren't any merits that pose a problem, Affinities vary a bit in quality but those that are bad for a concept are usually obviously useless at the concept stage (i.e. if you don't see a need to jump really far, don't get Falcon Soul Aloft) rather than bad in the implementation of the mechanics, and I think there was only one Utterance in the entire game that didn't really gel mechanically (Waters of Life). That's not to say all powers are equal, but it is very hard to make a Mummy who can't contribute to a party. So it's not an impossible demand by any means.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't really say anything on this subject because I haven't read Mummy. Ironically so, because the whole reason I haven't gotten into Mummy is that it's 1e and 1e has deep, deep, system-level issues with these exact same exp efficiency discrepencies we've been discussing and that puts me off the system. The difference to me is, I can ban or house rule Merits and splat powers that I find cause these problems, but when fundamental parts of the game like exponential exp costs cause these problems they're more trouble than they're worth for me to fix.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827943#post827943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Taking the Dual Kith always used to lead to you having fewer dots in Wyrd/Hollow/Fighting Style. And in first edition, Fighting Style was arguably a bigger deal than it is now. However, all those are things you can pick up as the game progresses. Kiths as representation of the Durance may put pressure on mechanically minded players to take it at character creation. Kiths that draw on Wyrd as the basis of their strength become an increasingly stronger investment as the game goes on. Small changes at character creation can lead to impossibly vast differences at the late game, something that is going to be very hard to judge when the possible combinations are as immense as they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but as I said I didn't find 1e Dual-Kith to be an issue because of power discrepancies, it was a problem for me because it became the &quot;play a Kith with a different Seeming&quot; Merit, and that made it a concept tax. Since Kith isn't tied to Seeming in 2e, my problems with Dual-Kith have already been resolved. The critiques you make here really only apply to the character creation only version of Dual-Kith. I would think the simple solution would be to use the other version.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827943#post827943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">None of this is to say Dual Kith is actually going to be bad for this game and shouldn't be included. I'm just taking exception to the idea that balance should not be a serious, even primary, concern in that decision. After all, if you want beast-like attributes without a beast-like Kith/Seeming, just say that you have them or refluff an existing Kith. Not every aesthetic choice needs to be backed by mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly the reason I don't see Dual-Kith being an issue any more. You're no longer forced to take it to make certain character concepts work, so it becomes an actual choice instead of a tax. To me the argument that it still might be a non-choice due to character optimization concerns doesn't hold water because unlike games that lend themselves to char op like D&amp;D, there's no easy metric for what makes a character optimized. Sure, if I want to build a character that's specialized in, let's say, Social Maneuvering, it would be a strong choice to take a Kith that helps with that and Dual-Kith into another Kith that helps with that. But I could also spend those dots on Sympathetic and Pusher. Or some dots in Fast Talk. Or maybe I want to diversify a bit, cause my first Kith gives me all the Social Maneuvering skill I think I'll need. Maybe I don't want a cripplingly overspecialized character and I'd rather branch out into some Crafting abilities. Maybe I'll Dual Kith into Smith for that, or maybe I'll pick up Automotive Genius and Area of Expertise for my specialized Craft. From where I'm standing, the ability to mix and match Kith and Seeming without taking Dual Kith is exactly the the reason it's an actual choice now instead of a tax like it used to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-11-2016, 12:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T20:50:34-08:00","id":827964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827948#post827948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are several Kiths that provide benefits that would cost significantly more to buy with xp or that are equivalent to more than 3-4 dots worth of merits. (Like the example HelmsDerp provided.) There are also a couple Kiths which are underwhelming compared to 3-4 dots worth of merits. Dual Kith has the potential of exacerbating this issue when one player uses Dual Kith to take two highly optimal options (possibly made even more optimal through synergy) and another player takes one of the more sub-optimal Kiths. Then the ST is left in the unenviable position of telling one of the two players to modify their character so they can be somewhat more balanced or struggling to make sure the overpowered character doesn't constantly steal the limelight.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just don't see the problem here. Once again, it's not like this is the only Merit or trait in the game with the potential to give a character the same benefits as another Merit or trait and then some for less exp, and I haven't found those options to be a problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827948#post827948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm in favor of keeping Dual Kith, personally, but I think it needs to be at least 4 dots and come with a &amp;quot;requires ST approval&amp;quot; caveat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the &quot;requires ST approval&quot; caveat is kind of an unspoken rule that applies to all Merits. And all other character traits, for that matter. I could see an argument for Dual Kith costing 4 dots though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T21:18:59-08:00","id":827974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827959#post827959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's correct, but it's not specified as a human only Merit. Restricting it to only human characters is a perfectly reasonable ruling, but so is saying that it's available to anyone. It's presumably at least available to Demons since it's in their core book and not specified as being unavailable to them. But I digress.</div> </div> </div> </div>For sure, Demons have it. I'm running it at the moment and I've got a Demon player with the merit. Whether this is because it slipped through with Demon, or even whether the developers made a conscious decision to limit it is up in the air. As for any other supernatural? Well, the default assumption with CoD is &quot;Anything in the core book, and ask your ST about anything beyond that&quot;, and I feel that would hold for Vampires and Werewolves at the moment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827959#post827959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it's not reasonable to critique. I'm just saying, if these kinds of Merits are a problem for you, it's pretty much a fact of CofD you're going to need to learn to deal with.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I'm trying to get it as that what you say is absolutely true, but I'm not sure it adds to the conversation.<br /> &quot;This thing you have a problem with exists.&quot;<br /> &quot;Yes, it does. I'd rather not have more of it.&quot;<br /> Feels like we're talking across one another, is all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827959#post827959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is, I think, where our philosophies diverge. I don't think it should be the game's job to try to fix the group's problems. It constrains design and it's just generally not very effective, since the game rules can only attempt to deal with such problems preeptively, and they can't possibly anticipate the needs of every group. Better in my opinion to leave the design unconstrained by such concerns and provide solid advice for groups to deal with their own problems. That's a pretty fundamental game design philosophy division though, and I don't expect either of us to be able to change the other's mind, so this might be an agree to disagree kind of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I consider it far more a system problem than a group problem. I'm actually surprised that anyone would consider it a group problem. In any other kind of game, a balance issue is undisputedly a system problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827959#post827959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't really say anything on this subject because I haven't read it. Ironically so, because the whole reason I haven't gotten into Mummy is that it's 1e and 1e has deep, deep, system-level issues with these exact same exp efficiency discrepencies we've been discussing and that puts me off the system. The difference to me is, I can ban or house rule Merits and splat powers that I find cause these problems, but when fundamental parts of the game like exponential exp costs cause these problems they're more trouble than they're worth for me to fix.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't call that a fundamental part of the game. If it bothers you, do what was basically done in the 2E conversion. Multiply all experience costs by 3 and use that as the flat cost for everything. I can't think of anything that breaks in 1E if you do it.<br /> <br /> That said, I never had a big problem with the experience system in first edition. I kind of liked the way it encouraged you to spend your experience making jack-of-all-trade characters rather than min-maxing on specific stats. 2E doesn't go one way or the other though, which I suppose is better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827959#post827959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, but as I said I didn't find 1e Dual-Kith to be an issue because of power discrepancies, it was a problem for me because it became the &quot;play a Kith with a different Seeming&quot; Merit, and that made it a concept tax. Since Kith isn't tied to Seeming in 2e, my problems with Dual-Kith have already been resolved. The critiques you make here really only apply to the character creation only version of Dual-Kith. I would think the simple solution would be to use the other version.</div> </div> </div> </div>My perspective is admittedly a little skewed, because Dual Kith in 1E was partly responsible for the group's social character becoming a combat powerhouse that eclipsed both dedicated combat characters in our long-running Changeling campaign. Fun times.<br /> <br /> The issue is with anything you can spend experience or points on that is disproportionately effective, not with the character creation-only version. And &quot;use the other version&quot; is an odd argument. We're discussing a potential merit in 2E, aren't we? How many variations on Dual Kith have been written for the new rules?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827959#post827959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's exactly the reason I don't see Dual-Kith being an issue any more. You're no longer forced to take it to make certain character concepts work, so it becomes an actual choice instead of a tax. To me the argument that it still might be a non-choice due to character optimization concerns doesn't hold water because unlike games that lend themselves to char op like D&amp;D, there's no easy metric for what makes a character optimized. Sure, if I want to build a character that's specialized in, let's say, Social Maneuvering, it would be a strong choice to take a Kith that helps with that and Dual-Kith into another Kith that helps with that. But I could also spend those dots on Sympathetic and Pusher. Or some dots in Fast Talk. Or maybe I want to diversify a bit, cause my first Kith gives me all the Social Maneuvering skill I think I'll need. Maybe I don't want a cripplingly overspecialized character and I'd rather branch out into some Crafting abilities. Maybe I'll Dual Kith into Smirh for that, or maybe I'll pick up Automotive Genius and Area of Expertise for my specialized Craft. From where I'm standing, the ability to mix and match Kith and Seeming without taking Dual Kith is exactly the the reason it's an actual choice now instead of a tax like it used to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look, if Dual Kith is balanced within the system, then I have no problem with it. If other merits are viable choices, great. But let's not get into a situation where it is usually more efficient to buy Dual Kith than purchasing the merits individually. That was the case in 1E, where buying Dual Kith was usually a much better choice than many other merits (particularly as Wyrd increased).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T21:22:33-08:00","id":827976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827964#post827964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the &quot;requires ST approval&quot; caveat is kind of an unspoken rule that applies to all Merits. And all other character traits, for that matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was an explicit rule in 1e, actually. It's probably in 2e as well, but I haven't looked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T21:23:57-08:00","id":827977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827964#post827964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just don't see the problem here. Once again, it's not like this is the only Merit or trait in the game with the potential to give a character the same benefits as another Merit or trait and then some for less exp, and I haven't found those options to be a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are problematic when they create a &quot;one right way&quot; to build a character. Among those players who care about mechanics, it limits choice, rather than expand it.<br /> <br /> In a nutshell, no one is hurt by an attempt to keep &quot;obviously better&quot; powers, merits, etc. in check. People, and the game, can be hurt by not doing so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T21:24:46-08:00","id":827978,"title":"","content":"I don't see Chronicles of Darkness as a competitive experience where the players are expected to go head-to-head in a cage-match style where the 1-2 extra dice to your pools you get from optimizing really makes a difference. I'd much rather the developers spend time on crafting an interesting and compelling experience rather than spending a large chunk of their time and budget trying to make sure the game meets some arbitrary level of what constitutes &quot;balanced.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827977#post827977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those are problematic when they create a &quot;one right way&quot; to build a character. Among those players who care about mechanics, it limits choice, rather than expand it.<br /> <br /> In a nutshell, no one is hurt by an attempt to keep &quot;obviously better&quot; powers, merits, etc. in check. People, and the game, can be hurt by not doing so.</div> </div> </div> </div>You keep using that &quot;Build&quot; word, as if characters were only supposed to be numbers on paper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","user":"ReshyShira","date":". 02-11-2016, 12:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T21:31:32-08:00","id":827981,"title":"","content":"I'm curious, what dual kith combos were creating such dramatic problems for people in 1e? The kith blessing were generally much less potent, though I do remember a few exceptions.<br /> <br /> I already have my bet on the most breakable kith blessing for 2e though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T21:38:19-08:00","id":827986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827978#post827978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see Chronicles of Darkness as a competitive experience where the players are expected to go head-to-head in a cage-match style where the 1-2 extra dice to your pools you get from optimizing really makes a difference. I'd much rather the developers spend time on crafting an interesting and compelling experience rather than spending a large chunk of their time trying to make sure the game meets some arbitrary level of what constitutes &quot;balanced.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, so, I ran a long, long running Changeling campaign. At around the time the group was at Wyrd 4, it was markedly obvious that one member of the party was the best in social situations, the best at investigations and occult research, and the best at combat. It's not that the game was competitive. It's that outside of minor edge cases (crafting, academic research, that kind of thing), this player was the only one who needed to act. In combat the others could help, but it was always this one character's show. In anything that wasn't combat, they often didn't even get a chance to help out before he would sort things out on his own. The player was wonderful, great at playing his character, but it really did feel like the hero wandering around with his less competent hangers-on. It wasn't all the fault of Dual Kiths, not by a long shot (1E Changeling had a looooot of dud Contracts, for example), but Dual Kith did play a role.<br /> <br /> An arbitrary level of balance is important. The game doesn't need to be perfectly balanced, not by a long shot. But the developers should avoid anything that is just mathematically superior to any other choice they have written. I don't care if, say, you have a merit which makes you better at opening Doors and a merit which lets you do more damage, and the latter does more damage than the former opens Doors. But I do care if you write two powers which open Doors and one just does it better all the time. It means that there's a wrong choice at character creation, and any player who makes that choice is going to feel bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T21:42:02-08:00","id":827988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827981#post827981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious, what dual kith combos were creating such dramatic problems for people in 1e? The kith blessing were generally much less potent, though I do remember a few exceptions.<br /> <br /> I already have my bet on the most breakable kith blessing for 2e though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I actually never had a problem with it in 1e, myself. I'm only a little concerned about it because the 2e blessings are so much more potent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T21:42:20-08:00","id":827989,"title":"","content":"Okay. I lost the thread of this somehow.<br /> <br /> Is the problem that Dual Kith in the past seemed like such a no-brainer that it was something you had to get, akin to...I think it was Electroshock Therapy in Promethean or something?<br /> <br /> Better question here: what's going on? o_o","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T21:48:11-08:00","id":827990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827989#post827989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay. I lost the thread of this somehow.<br /> <br /> Is the problem that Dual Kith in the past seemed like such a no-brainer that it was something you had to get, akin to...I think it was Electroshock Therapy in Promethean or something?<br /> <br /> Better question here: what's going on? o_o</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Basically it seems like people are arguing about whether an unbalanced merit is a bug or a feature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T21:51:46-08:00","id":827993,"title":"","content":"At a lot of tables, the 1E Dual Kith merit was basically a no-brainer from both a creativity perspective (partially due to Kiths being tied to Seeming) and from a mechanical perspective to have a nice set of tricks. Hence some people feeling that it was either grossly overpowered compared to the other options for your creation merit dots and other people basically feeling that it was a merit dot tax to build an effective changeling because there's no reason to not take it.<br /> <br /> The rest of the discussion is basically attempting to reconcile different philosophies of how game balance should work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T22:02:13-08:00","id":827999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827974#post827974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I'm trying to get it as that what you say is absolutely true, but I'm not sure it adds to the conversation.<br /> &amp;quot;This thing you have a problem with exists.&amp;quot;<br /> &amp;quot;Yes, it does. I'd rather not have more of it.&amp;quot;<br /> Feels like we're talking across one another, is all.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I'm trying to get at is that the evidence suggests that's not a concern the developers take into heavy consideration. You might want to take a different approach with your critique.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827974#post827974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I consider it far more a system problem than a group problem. I'm actually surprised that anyone would consider it a group problem. In any other kind of game, a balance issue is undisputedly a system problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, I think we're at an impasse here. I'm comfortable leaving this particular line of discussion at that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827974#post827974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't call that a fundamental part of the game. If it bothers you, do what was basically done in the 2E conversion. Multiply all experience costs by 3 and use that as the flat cost for everything. I can't think of anything that breaks in 1E if you do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's what I would do if I was going to run 1e again. Or, technically I'd find the mean cost per dot and make that the cost for each dot, which is how the math works out for 2e costs as well. But again, I digress.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827974#post827974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I never had a big problem with the experience system in first edition. I kind of liked the way it encouraged you to spend your experience making jack-of-all-trade characters rather than min-maxing on specific stats. 2E doesn't go one way or the other though, which I suppose is better.</div> </div> </div> </div>It only encourages the jack of all trades thing post character creation. At character creation you get a set number of free dots that don't account for the scaling mechanic apart from the fact that the 5th dot of everything cost two of your free dots. In effect, it means players that put as many dots as possible in the smallest number of traits end up dozens or even scores of exp ahead of players that diversify, encouraging serious min-maxing. The scaling costs also lead to a lot of weird interactions that required a certain degree of system mastery to work out, like how it's always best to spend 6 starting Merit dots on Power Stat if you plan to raise it at all or none otherwise, or how vampires should always alternate between raising actual Stamina and raising Resilience (that one is specific to MET, but it's still part of the same problem).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827974#post827974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My perspective is admittedly a little skewed, because Dual Kith in 1E was partly responsible for the group's social character becoming a combat powerhouse that eclipsed both dedicated combat characters in our long-running Changeling campaign. Fun times.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like a really interesting story, but yeah I can see how that would sour the idea of the Merit for you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827974#post827974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue is with anything you can spend experience or points on that is disproportionately effective, not with the character creation-only version. And &amp;quot;use the other version&amp;quot; is an odd argument. We're discussing a potential merit in 2E, aren't we? How many variations on Dual Kith have been written for the new rules?</div> </div> </div> </div>What I'm trying to say is that it's very difficult to define &quot;effective&quot; in CofD, so it makes &quot;disproportionately effective&quot; a weak critique in my mind. And I was suggesting that since your arguments seemed to be focused on the fact that you take Kiths at character creation that the 2e version of the Merit could address them by just not having that restriction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827974#post827974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look, if Dual Kith is balanced within the system, then I have no problem with it. If other merits are viable choices, great. But let's not get into a situation where it is usually more efficient to buy Dual Kith than purchasing the merits individually. That was the case in 1E, where buying Dual Kith was usually a much better choice than many other merits (particularly as Wyrd increased).</div> </div> </div> </div>What I'm trying to get at is that it's very difficult to define &quot;balanced&quot; or &quot;efficient&quot; within CofD because everything is so context dependent. Dual Kith is a great choice for certain character concepts (or character builds, if you're the &quot;build&quot; sort), and not as great for others. That would have been the case in 1e too, in my opinion, had it not been for the fact that you absolutely needed it if the Kith you wanted wasn't attached to the Seeming you wanted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827977#post827977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those are problematic when they create a &amp;quot;one right way&amp;quot; to build a character. Among those players who care about mechanics, it limits choice, rather than expand it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think there can be a &quot;one right way&quot; to build a character in CofD because there's no clear metric for what makes a character &quot;effective&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827977#post827977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a nutshell, no one is hurt by an attempt to keep &amp;quot;obviously better&amp;quot; powers, merits, etc. in check. People, and the game, can be hurt by not doing so.</div> </div> </div> </div>If keeping &quot;obviously better&quot; powers in check means removing powers that significantly expand options for character concepts, then yes, people are hurt by it. Namely, the people who would have enjoyed playing the concepts those options would have enabled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T22:08:19-08:00","id":828000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827986#post827986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An arbitrary level of balance is important. The game doesn't need to be perfectly balanced, not by a long shot. But the developers should avoid anything that is just mathematically superior to any other choice they have written. I don't care if, say, you have a merit which makes you better at opening Doors and a merit which lets you do more damage, and the latter does more damage than the former opens Doors. But I do care if you write two powers which open Doors and one just does it better all the time. It means that there's a wrong choice at character creation, and any player who makes that choice is going to feel bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're going to be disappointed when all things are not mathematically formulaic when it comes to mechanical benefits. CofD is a game that incentivizes, to some level, taking certain merits that have roleplaying implications and expectations for greater mechanical benefit. Roleplaying your sympathetic character is much more appealing than having simply another dot or two in the relevant skill in a pool that is already over 9. It's almost like the &quot;Skill&quot; of Chronicles of Darkness is roleplaying potential. If it adds to the roleplaying potential then it's more likely to be more mechanically beneficial in general than just increasing a flat attribute with no real face or meaning besides being a number.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T22:16:07-08:00","id":828004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827981#post827981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious, what dual kith combos were creating such dramatic problems for people in 1e? The kith blessing were generally much less potent, though I do remember a few exceptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, it was never a problem with Kiths or the powers they granted. I don't really um... care about that. The problem was if you wanted to play, say, a character who was a living flame but you also wanted to have wings, Dual Kith was essential. It was the mix-and-match Kith and Seeming Merit, the second Kith was often incidental. In effect, players who wanted a concept that didn't fit into one of the boxes of the available Kiths paired with their default Seemings (which was, to be fair, a lot of boxes but still) had to start three Merit dots behind players who wanted a concept that did fit a pre-existing Kith. Which, with the skewed incentives scaling xp costs caused, was a positively tremendous problem.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827989#post827989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay. I lost the thread of this somehow.<br /> <br /> Is the problem that Dual Kith in the past seemed like such a no-brainer that it was something you had to get, akin to...I think it was Electroshock Therapy in Promethean or something?<br /> <br /> Better question here: what's going on? o_o</div> </div> </div> </div>That's part of it, but that particular discussion is just kind of illustrative of the kinds of issues we're arguing about. Basically, we're discussing whether or not<br /> <br /> a.) Merits and other character elements that give you similar benefits to or greater benefits than other character elements for less exp a problem that the game should be designed to curtail or not. (Resilience and Vigor in vampire are a good example; they give all the same benefits as raising their associated attributes, plus some other cool abilities, for the same cost out-of-clan or less exp in-clan)<br /> <br /> and<br /> <br /> b.) Is Dual Kith one such Merit?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827990#post827990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically it seems like people are arguing about whether an unbalanced merit is a bug or a feature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Er... Kind of, but it's a bit more complex than that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827993#post827993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At a lot of tables, the 1E Dual Kith merit was basically a no-brainer from both a creativity perspective (partially due to Kiths being tied to Seeming) and from a mechanical perspective to have a nice set of tricks. Hence some people feeling that it was either grossly overpowered compared to the other options for your creation merit dots and other people basically feeling that it was a merit dot tax to build an effective changeling because there's no reason to not take it.<br /> <br /> The rest of the discussion is basically attempting to reconcile different philosophies of how game balance should work.</div> </div> </div> </div>^^^ This guy gets it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-11-2016, 01:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T22:18:50-08:00","id":828005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827999#post827999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I'm trying to get at is that the evidence suggests that's not a concern the developers take into heavy consideration. You might want to take a different approach with your critique.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whether or not they do is sort of irrelevant as to whether they should or will do in the future. Let's assume I have hope at least some of this may be considered.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827999#post827999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I said, I think we're at an impasse here. I'm comfortable leaving this particular line of discussion at that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. Count me baffled though <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827999#post827999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that's what I would do if I was going to run 1e again. Or, technically I'd find the mean cost per dot and make that the cost for each dot, which is how the math works out for 2e costs as well. But again, I digress.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's the multiply by 3 thing. Everything costs like the 3rd dot should cost. Or something.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827999#post827999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It only encourages the jack of all trades thing post character creation. At character creation you get a set number of free dots that don't account for the scaling mechanic apart from the fact that the 5th dot of everything cost two of your free dots. In effect, it means players that put as many dots as possible in the smallest number of traits end up dozens or even scores of exp ahead of players that diversify, encouraging serious min-maxing. The scaling costs also lead to a lot of weird interactions that required a certain degree of system mastery to work out, like how it's always best to spend 6 starting Merit dots on Power Stat if you plan to raise it at all or none otherwise, or how vampires should always alternate between raising actual Stamina and raising Resilience (that one is specific to MET, but it's still part of the same problem).</div> </div> </div> </div>Strictly speaking, yes, that was the most efficient experience-wise to do something. If you ever intended raising something above starting traits, start with it as high as you can. But the flipside is that everything still just gives you one dice.<br /> <br /> But yes, not ideal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827999#post827999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I'm trying to say is that it's very difficult to define &quot;effective&quot; in CofD, so it makes &quot;disproportionately effective&quot; a weak critique in my mind. And I was suggesting that since your arguments seemed to be focused on the fact that you take Kiths at character creation that the 2e version of the Merit could address them by just not having that restriction.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, my argument is really based on whether or not a second Kith will be a better option than an equivalent merit. Doesn't matter when it's purchased if it's a no-brainer everyone could or should get.<br /> <br /> But it certainly is worse if someone makes a mistake at character creation and can't rectify it later. At least Goblin Markets provide an in-universe excuse to fix it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827999#post827999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I'm trying to get at is that it's very difficult to define &quot;balanced&quot; or &quot;efficient&quot; within CofD because everything is so context dependent. Dual Kith is a great choice for certain character concepts (or character builds, if you're the &quot;build&quot; sort), and not as great for others. That would have been the case in 1e too, in my opinion, had it not been for the fact that you absolutely needed it if the Kith you wanted wasn't attached to the Seeming you wanted.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not that difficult. If someone rolls more dice to do a thing than someone else, they're better at it. If both characters spent the same amount of experience on, say, being good at combat, and one of them is clearly better at it, then that is clearly a more efficient build. There, definition established.<br /> <br /> The new, more clearly defined rules for things like Social Maneuvering mean that even social interactions aren't quite so nebulous. Context is important, but it's hardly everything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827999#post827999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If keeping &quot;obviously better&quot; powers in check means removing powers that significantly expand options for character concepts, then yes, people are hurt by it. Namely, the people who would have enjoyed playing the concepts those options would have enabled.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually not advocating removing Dual Kith. I'm just saying that I hope that, if it does make it in, that it's priced appropriately and isn't a clearly better choice than an equivalent merit. I hope that a merit that gives the option for such a startling array of choices is given due consideration before implementation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T22:28:43-08:00","id":828011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827993#post827993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[...]and other people basically feeling that it was a merit dot tax to build an effective changeling because there's no reason to not take it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll be honest, with the sheer popularity of the merit, I'd actually rather see it become the default, and if you choose not have multiple kiths you're compensated with bonus experiences that can be spent on whatever. Because, frankly, I find the idea of playing a dual/triple kithed Changeling so much more interesting to roleplay than anything else that it's doubtful I won't ever take it. And, it seems to me, that many people agree with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=828005#post828005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not that difficult. If someone rolls more dice to do a thing than someone else, they're better at it. If both characters spent the same amount of experience on, say, being good at combat, and one of them is clearly better at it, then that is clearly a more efficient build. There, definition established.<br /> <br /> The new, more clearly defined rules for things like Social Maneuvering mean that even social interactions aren't quite so nebulous. Context is important, but it's hardly everything.<br /> <br /> I'm actually not advocating removing Dual Kith. I'm just saying that I hope that, if it does make it in, that it's priced appropriately and isn't a clearly better choice than an equivalent merit. I hope that a merit that gives the option for such a startling array of choices is given due consideration before implementation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Azahul, let me ask you something. When you raise a stat, say Strength from 3 to 4, what really changes on your character sheet? Because, in my experience, the dice pool itself means precisely jack from a roleplaying perspective. It's just a metric of effectiveness, it doesn't create interest in the character.<br /> <br /> Your character selling part of their soul or being biologically augmented on a lab table for that point of strength, however, that's much more interesting. That's something you can roleplay out and actually have be relevant to the game itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","user":"ReshyShira","date":". 02-11-2016, 01:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T22:36:01-08:00","id":828013,"title":"","content":"Yeah, no. Don't get me wrong, I get the appeal, but there's some design restrictions that come from the subject matter themselves on that one.<br /> <br /> Still, got the gist of the issue. I don't think I wanna mess around on this one. As y'all were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T22:37:32-08:00","id":828014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=828005#post828005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, my argument is really based on whether or not a second Kith will be a better option than an equivalent merit. Doesn't matter when it's purchased if it's a no-brainer everyone could or should get.<br /> <br /> But it certainly is worse if someone makes a mistake at character creation and can't rectify it later. At least Goblin Markets provide an in-universe excuse to fix it.<br /> <br /> It's not that difficult. If someone rolls more dice to do a thing than someone else, they're better at it. If both characters spent the same amount of experience on, say, being good at combat, and one of them is clearly better at it, then that is clearly a more efficient build. There, definition established.<br /> <br /> The new, more clearly defined rules for things like Social Maneuvering mean that even social interactions aren't quite so nebulous. Context is important, but it's hardly everything.<br /> <br /> I'm actually not advocating removing Dual Kith. I'm just saying that I hope that, if it does make it in, that it's priced appropriately and isn't a clearly better choice than an equivalent merit. I hope that a merit that gives the option for such a startling array of choices is given due consideration before implementation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, let's just say, hypothetically, the Kiths that have been spoiled make it into the book as written, and the ones we haven't seen yet fall into the same range of power (however you care to define it) as the ones we have seen so far. How many dots would Dual-Kith need to cost to make it fair in your assessment? We've got several books of Merits to compare to to find equivalents, so if it's not that hard to define what makes a character effective, you should be able to work out what it should cost. Assume it has no prerequisites, and if the cost you determine is appropriate would be greater than 5 dots, what prerequisites would you suggest adding to it to bring it down to 5 dots or less?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-11-2016, 01:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T22:37:54-08:00","id":828016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=828013#post828013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, no. Don't get me wrong, I get the appeal, but there's some design restrictions that come from the subject matter themselves on that one.<br /> <br /> Still, got the gist of the issue. I don't think I wanna mess around on this one. As y'all were.</div> </div> </div> </div>That in reference to making multi-kithing the default?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T22:39:26-08:00","id":828017,"title":"","content":"Yes. Multi-kithing can't be the default because fairies don't often work that way, in a nutshell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T22:41:16-08:00","id":828019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827978#post827978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see Chronicles of Darkness as a competitive experience where the players are expected to go head-to-head in a cage-match style where the 1-2 extra dice to your pools you get from optimizing really makes a difference. I'd much rather the developers spend time on crafting an interesting and compelling experience rather than spending a large chunk of their time and budget trying to make sure the game meets some arbitrary level of what constitutes &quot;balanced.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok.<br /> <br /> The games? They're not just for you. &quot;This isn't a problem for my playstyle, so it isn't a problem,&quot; is a bullshit argument. It's just saying that everyone that doesn't approach the games like you do, should be ignored by the game designers. It isn't actually making a good point about the games, or about more general theories on design.<br /> <br /> Also, a lot of us don't have the fortune of groups that don't care about mechanical oddities. We have to play with the people we have, which means doing our best to find games that work for the group. If the developers did what you said, a lot of people that want to play CofD wouldn't because their groups would have to compromise for games that manage to offer interesting and compelling experience <i>and</i> have some mechanical rigor.<br /> <br /> Besides that, for a lot of people, &quot;crafting an interesting and compelling experience,&quot; in an RPG requires spending development on mechanical rigor to have the concepts and the rules work together.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You keep using that &quot;Build&quot; word, as if characters were only supposed to be numbers on paper. </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> Seriously. What the fuck? Why do you keep making these extremely disingenuous insinuations? When people say &quot;build,&quot; they mean how a character is mechanically built using the system. That's all. They don't mean &quot;I don't care about role-playing my character.&quot; Suggesting that people that talk about builds don't care about role-playing is nothing but bad faith.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=827989#post827989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the problem that Dual Kith in the past seemed like such a no-brainer that it was something you had to get, akin to...I think it was Electroshock Therapy in Promethean or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the big mechanical problem with it from 1e; though a bit more complicated than that example since it usually was a bit more specific to a given character focus. As Charlaquin pointed out, there was also the &quot;concept tax&quot; for wanting a Seeming/Kith combination that 1e didn't allow without the Merit, but we already know 2e eliminated that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T22:43:48-08:00","id":828020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=828017#post828017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. Multi-kithing can't be the default because fairies don't often work that way, in a nutshell.</div> </div> </div> </div>In practice though, it seems like most PC changelings would be multi-kithed, at least from what seems to be the general consensus. Would it be possible to include a variant rule that kind of allows or sets the foundation for that kind of thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T22:47:36-08:00","id":828023,"title":"","content":"Seems easier and more appropriate to house rule that sort of thing. Popularity isn't always a good reason to do things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T22:49:40-08:00","id":828024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=828023#post828023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems easier and more appropriate to house rule that sort of thing. Popularity isn't always a good reason to do things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh well, well I do hope that the creativity tax isn't too high then.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Would like to see a Third-Kith be an option, even if it costs more merit dots than the dual-kith, just to have that option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T22:55:30-08:00","id":828027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=828011#post828011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll be honest, with the sheer popularity of the merit, I'd actually rather see it become the default, and if you choose not have multiple kiths you're compensated with bonus experiences that can be spent on whatever. Because, frankly, I find the idea of playing a dual/triple kithed Changeling so much more interesting to roleplay than anything else that it's doubtful I won't ever take it. And, it seems to me, that many people agree with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Playing devil's advocate for a second, this right here? This is exactly what Heavy Arms and Azahul are worried about. And frankly, if this was how it was, I would agree with them whole-heartedly. If the Merit is so ubiquitously auto-chosen, it should just be part of the template. And it absolutely, positively should not just be part of the template. <br /> <br /> Fortunately, I don't think that will be the case. There are lots of options for customizing characters' Kith(s), so it's not essential to pick it just to get the concept you want, which makes it a largely mechanical and aesthetic choice. And there are plenty of other mechanical and aesthetic options at similar prices that are worth considering, even before taking into account any new Merits that Changeling may include. So I don't think these concerns are unfounded, but I think those that hold them will be satisfied. Hopefully.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T23:09:25-08:00","id":828032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=828027#post828027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Playing devil's advocate for a second, this right here? This is exactly what Heavy Arms and Azahul are worried about. And frankly, if this was how it was, I would agree with them whole-heartedly. If the Merit is so ubiquitously auto-chosen, it should just be part of the template. And it absolutely, positively should not just be part of the template.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, I don't think that will be the case. There are lots of options for customizing characters' Kith(s), so it's not essential to pick it just to get the concept you want, which makes it a largely mechanical and aesthetic choice. And there are plenty of other mechanical and aesthetic options at similar prices that are worth considering, even before taking into account any new Merits that Changeling may include. So I don't think these concerns are unfounded, but I think those that hold them will be satisfied. Hopefully.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haven't played Changeling 2e, so I guess that still remains to be seen. I'm the kind of player that likes mixing flavors of different things to get interesting results. So I'm exactly the kind of individual that would be all over multi-kithing merits. Seems like a lot of people are of the same opinion, or at least the ones that seem to be in the circles here. Who knows, maybe I'm just a weird freak when it comes to how I like my characters (Typically the more monstrous the better).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T23:34:43-08:00","id":828037,"title":"","content":"It would be moderately insane of me to try and say that Dual-Kith <i>wasn't</i> popular. I once spent time figuring out how to get six kiths for one character.<br /> <br /> But, as I mentioned, popularity can be a poor reason to do something, even as a suggested hack. We have an aesthetic and an atmosphere to sell, and the ideas and attitudes behind Kiths are part and parcel for that. We have to stay true to what stories we're drawing from, as well as how we shape it and sell it back.<br /> <br /> Dual-Kith lets people break the mold as best fits the characters while still making the appeal to the skeleton stories we started with. If people want to figure out the ways to break the game and let in more, kudos. I'm not going to tell you that's invalid, and if people can find the readings that allows for six kiths and want to go for it, then I give my blessing.<br /> <br /> But as a general rule, one is the norm, with two being a reasonable exception. Any more than that, and Changeling loses one of it's subtler but quite powerful undercurrents to a customization that beds an absurdism out of place for Changeling, and maybe WoD on the whole given the context. Three or more should either be rare, or a table reading of the rules, in the same vein as that one trick I looked up ages ago. It should never seem to be a thing to happen at every table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T23:57:33-08:00","id":828042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=828014#post828014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, let's just say, hypothetically, the Kiths that have been spoiled make it into the book as written, and the ones we haven't seen yet fall into the same range of power (however you care to define it) as the ones we have seen so far. How many dots would Dual-Kith need to cost to make it fair in your assessment? We've got several books of Merits to compare to to find equivalents, so if it's not that hard to define what makes a character effective, you should be able to work out what it should cost. Assume it has no prerequisites, and if the cost you determine is appropriate would be greater than 5 dots, what prerequisites would you suggest adding to it to bring it down to 5 dots or less?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm guessing you're directing this question at Azahul, but I'd like to chime in. It's tricky because a handful of the Kiths we've seen seem like 3 dots would be plenty and, on the other hand, many of them would be a bargain at 5 dots. Which is why I've been saying 4 dots - seems like a reasonable compromise to me. After reading the recently spoiled Clarity rules, I'd also say that Dual Kith should come packaged with an additional Trigger. Given how Clarity works, that's not exactly a huge drawback, but it adds a complication that I think is appropriate for what Dual Kith represents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T00:24:20-08:00","id":828047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=828042#post828042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm guessing you're directing this question at Azahul, but I'd like to chime in. It's tricky because a handful of the Kiths we've seen seem like 3 dots would be plenty and, on the other hand, many of them would be a bargain at 5 dots. Which is why I've been saying 4 dots - seems like a reasonable compromise to me. After reading the recently spoiled Clarity rules, I'd also say that Dual Kith should come packaged with an additional Trigger. Given how Clarity works, that's not exactly a huge drawback, but it adds a complication that I think is appropriate for what Dual Kith represents.</div> </div> </div> </div>Five plus the drawback seems pretty fair to me. I'm cleaned to hew to the higher end of the spectrum simply because some of the Kiths are so good. I'd rather balance towards the higher end of the spectrum, because striking a compromise actually does give a clear advantage to taking the merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T00:37:53-08:00","id":828051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=828042#post828042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm guessing you're directing this question at Azahul, but I'd like to chime in. It's tricky because a handful of the Kiths we've seen seem like 3 dots would be plenty and, on the other hand, many of them would be a bargain at 5 dots. Which is why I've been saying 4 dots - seems like a reasonable compromise to me. After reading the recently spoiled Clarity rules, I'd also say that Dual Kith should come packaged with an additional Trigger. Given how Clarity works, that's not exactly a huge drawback, but it adds a complication that I think is appropriate for what Dual Kith represents.</div> </div> </div> </div>An additional trigger would actually be an interesting concept to try out, and for me it also ties in well to the character that sparked this whole thread off. His Gentry basically took a look at the superhero genre and decided that it would be interesting to see what happens if heroes and monsters fought over civilians, and &quot;employed&quot; humans who came/were brought to its domain as &quot;Actors&quot; to be civilians, monsters or heroes, without any of the sugarcoating that shows like Power Rangers would imply. Monsters killed and gored civilians, heroes and sometimes each other; civilians turned on one another to stay alive yet to stay in the limelight; heroes were given new personalities that often caused them to fight each other, even as they helped fight the monsters to keep the civilians &quot;safe&quot;. The only way to get food and water in that domain is to be observed in the conflicts that the Gentry set up, and though anyone who got caught up in the fight would be patched up and revived once a surviving side was made, which incentivizes the participants to come into the fray in spite of the horrible pain it normally inflicts. The only exceptions are the heroes, who are repaired but never revived if killed (since heroes, by being &quot;heroic&quot;, stayed dead, but come back with new powers if merely maimed) and are deposited into the fray by default.<br /> <br /> This has left my character split on what he has become. On the one hand, his Airtouched aspect is fine by him, as it is his choice to do with it as he wishes and it is effectively a physical enhancement. His Playmate side however? That's purely cooperative and as such it influences his behavior, something that sparked his departure from his Keeper (he realized after reading the various recountings/&quot;synopsis&quot; of his past battles that in spite of remembering those fights, his &quot;story&quot; made no goddamn sense due to his &quot;character&quot; changing each time). Though working together with others is normally a good thing, and he is stronger for doing so, it reminds him of the time he was a part of the masses doing things that assisted the &quot;heroes&quot; and &quot;civilians&quot;. He can't even take being called &quot;heroic&quot; because of the association he has with that, even though by default he wants to help people since, unlike in his Keeper's domain, normal people don't get up again if slain.<br /> <br /> I suppose I could make a kith that would fit that kind of character, or just take Airtouched or Playmate to fit it, but the themes they represent (and the fact he's kind of a tribute to Kamen Rider) makes me really just want to take both kiths. I'd be all for another trigger for both of those kiths because it better emphasizes the struggle he has with his past and his own desires, and it's the kind of struggle I'd like to play out.<br /> <br /> tldr: I agree with this idea since it can be used to bring more to characters than the merit alone could. You are also free to ignore my ranting about a character who has not yet been committed to a game or even a proper character sheet. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T01:13:13-08:00","id":828059,"title":"","content":"Things like additional triggers for Clarity are the kind of &quot;costs&quot; I was talking about earlier in the thread on how estimating how much Dual Kith should be worth is more than just trying to line up Merits dots.<br /> <br /> It is absolutely the kind of thing I'd like to see for it rather than haggling about 4 dots vs. 5 dots (1 XP... just doesn't mean that much), because it's not just about any sort of balance argument in terms of strict mechanics, but more of a conceptual balance of a mixed Kith coming with more than just all perks, but some drawbacks to make the balance of two Kiths in one changeling something with greater story potential in both directions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T06:53:21-08:00","id":828197,"title":"","content":"I really like the idea of 4 dots and an additional trigger.<br /> <br /> Also, to weigh in on the build vs roleplay side... no. It's not a binary. Mechanics should inform the roleplay, and vice versa. If your character concept involves being really good at a particular skill, but your choice of abilities make you less capable at it than someone who ostensibly doesn't specialize in that area but picked better merits, that's going to be incredibly frustrating. Sure, you can tell a really good story about coming to terms with mediocrity, but that should be because that's the story you want to tell, not because poor dice pools keep forcing it on you. <br /> <br /> And honestly, I have an easier time starting from the mechanics side. I'll see a couple of merits or contracts that have an interesting interaction and work that into a concept, thinking about what kind of person would invest in those abilities, or what kind of durance would lead to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T07:01:00-08:00","id":828200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=828197#post828197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like the idea of 4 dots and an additional trigger.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually like that a lot as well. The additional Trigger is a good non-exp drawback for the Merit, and it feels versimilar given what Kith means and how they are acquired.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=828197#post828197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, to weigh in on the build vs roleplay side... no. It's not a binary. Mechanics should inform the roleplay, and vice versa. If your character concept involves being really good at a particular skill, but your choice of abilities make you less capable at it than someone who ostensibly doesn't specialize in that area but picked better merits, that's going to be incredibly frustrating. Sure, you can tell a really good story about coming to terms with mediocrity, but that should be because that's the story you want to tell, not because poor dice pools keep forcing it on you.<br /> <br /> And honestly, I have an easier time starting from the mechanics side. I'll see a couple of merits or contracts that have an interesting interaction and work that into a concept, thinking about what kind of person would invest in those abilities, or what kind of durance would lead to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anyone meant to suggest that it's binary. I certainly didn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T07:37:59-08:00","id":828213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=828032#post828032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Haven't played Changeling 2e, so I guess that still remains to be seen. I'm the kind of player that likes mixing flavors of different things to get interesting results. So I'm exactly the kind of individual that would be all over multi-kithing merits. Seems like a lot of people are of the same opinion, or at least the ones that seem to be in the circles here. Who knows, maybe I'm just a weird freak when it comes to how I like my characters (Typically the more monstrous the better).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, lots of people like the Merit, and that's a great thing. As long as it's a choice. You should decide that because you like mixing flavors of different things to get interesting results, Dual Kith is worth the opportunity cost. What people don't want to happen is for Dual Kith to be the Merit that everyone automatically takes without considering other options because it's that much of a no-brainer. I mean, if it's a no-brainer for you because you like that kind of play so much, that's fine. It becomes a problem when it's a no-brainer for everyone, even people who would otherwise probably play a Single-Kith character.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, I don't think that will happen. It does seem I have a higher tolerance for especially exp efficient Merits than some of the folks here, so my assessment has some margin for error. But I still think the Merit will sit in a good place cost wise for most people to not feel it's obligatory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T07:50:47-08:00","id":828216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=828037#post828037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But as a general rule, one is the norm, with two being a reasonable exception. Any more than that, and Changeling loses one of it's subtler but quite powerful undercurrents to a customization that beds an absurdism out of place for Changeling, and maybe WoD on the whole given the context. Three or more should either be rare, or a table reading of the rules, in the same vein as that one trick I looked up ages ago. It should never seem to be a thing to happen at every table.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I do hope there will still be opportunities for gathering additional Kiths for those who want them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=828200#post828200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually like that a lot as well. The additional Trigger is a good non-exp drawback for the Merit, and it feels versimilar given what Kith means and how they are acquired.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd think I'd like to see it in this form, no experiences for the second kith, instead you gotta deal with having another trigger condition out of the gate. Probably a reflection of having more duties and a greater warping of yourself as part of the durance.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=828213#post828213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, lots of people like the Merit, and that's a great thing. As long as it's a choice. You should decide that because you like mixing flavors of different things to get interesting results, Dual Kith is worth the opportunity cost. What people don't want to happen is for Dual Kith to be the Merit that everyone automatically takes without considering other options because it's that much of a no-brainer. I mean, if it's a no-brainer for you because you like that kind of play so much, that's fine. It becomes a problem when it's a no-brainer for everyone, even people who would otherwise probably play a Single-Kith character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, it's not about it being a no brainer, it's that people seem to enjoy mixing flavors. I do it all the time. It's not so much that it's binary or required but that it's simply a highly appealing choice creatively speaking.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=828213#post828213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does seem I have a higher tolerance for especially exp efficient Merits than some of the folks here, so my assessment has some margin for error. But I still think the Merit will sit in a good place cost wise for most people to not feel it's obligatory.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really see it that way. Most of the merits with the most mechanical edge are also the ones with higher roleplaying expectations. Adding a dot to persuasion is far less interesting than roleplaying out the Sympathetic merit. The difference between having Presence 4 and 5 is miniscule compared to being the Gargantuan kith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T08:13:33-08:00","id":828225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=828216#post828216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd think I'd like to see it in this form, no experiences for the second kith, instead you gotta deal with having another trigger condition out of the gate. Probably a reflection of having more duties and a greater warping of yourself as part of the durance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't make it free, but I think the extra trigger is a good drawback on top of the dot cost, if one is needed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=828216#post828216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, it's not about it being a no brainer, it's that people seem to enjoy mixing flavors. I do it all the time. It's not so much that it's binary or required but that it's simply a highly appealing choice creatively speaking.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that's exactly what it's about for the people arguing against it in this thread. If it's a highly appealing Merit because it allows you to mix-and-match people enjoy doing that, that's fine. If it's a no-brainer because it gets you the most value for its cost regardless of character concept, that's a problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=828216#post828216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really see it that way. Most of the merits with the most mechanical edge are also the ones with higher roleplaying expectations. Adding a dot to persuasion is far less interesting than roleplaying out the Sympathetic merit. The difference between having Presence 4 and 5 is miniscule compared to being the Gargantuan kith.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I agree that roleplaying is often a good enough opportunity cost for efficient Merits (see Professional Training). But people have had issues in the past with 1e Dual Kith's value far exceeding its opportunity cost, and it's not unreasonable to be wary of the same thing happening again. I will reiterate once more that I don't think this will happen, but my tolerance for this sort of thing appears to be higher than that of many of the Dual-Kith detractors in this thread, so it's entirely possible that while I think Dual Kith is in a fine place as it stands in the drafts, they might not agree with me if they read the drafts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T08:20:01-08:00","id":828228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=828213#post828213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does seem I have a higher tolerance for especially exp efficient Merits than some of the folks here, so my assessment has some margin for error. But I still think the Merit will sit in a good place cost wise for most people to not feel it's obligatory.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have a problem with Professional Training or Mystery Cult Initiation, which I think are the most xp efficient merits. The thing is that some (not all) of the Kiths provide merits that are significantly unbalanced even compared to PT or MCI. Hell, one of the Kiths includes PT along with other benefits. I don't expect, or even want, perfect mechanical balance, but there is still such a thing as <i>too</i> unbalanced. At 3 dots with no drawbacks, I think it would quickly become the default for most characters; it's just too good to pass up. I think even at 4 dots and an extra trigger it'll be super common.<br /> <br /> <br /> (I'm glad people seem to like my 4 dots and an extra trigger idea.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T08:31:23-08:00","id":828232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=828228#post828228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't have a problem with Professional Training or Mystery Cult Initiation, which I think are the most xp efficient merits. The thing is that some (not all) of the Kiths provide merits that are significantly unbalanced even compared to PT or MCI. Hell, one of the Kiths includes PT along with other benefits. I don't expect, or even want, perfect mechanical balance, but there is still such a thing as <i>too</i> unbalanced. At 3 dots with no drawbacks, I think it would quickly become the default for most characters; it's just too good to pass up. I think even at 4 dots and an extra trigger it'll be super common.<br /> <br /> <br /> (I'm glad people seem to like my 4 dots and an extra trigger idea.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Not all of the kiths are so powerful though. Making it too expensive for the &quot;weaker&quot; kiths could be punishing. Then it becomes a tax on creativity because the merit's cost is determined based on the most &quot;powerful&quot; kiths. I don't think it should be assumed that merit will be used exclusively to take the &quot;best&quot; kiths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T08:33:48-08:00","id":828234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=828228#post828228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have a problem with Professional Training or Mystery Cult Initiation, which I think are the most xp efficient merits. The thing is that some (not all) of the Kiths provide merits that are significantly unbalanced even compared to PT or MCI. Hell, one of the Kiths includes PT along with other benefits. I don't expect, or even want, perfect mechanical balance, but there is still such a thing as <i>too</i> unbalanced. At 3 dots with no drawbacks, I think it would quickly become the default for most characters; it's just too good to pass up. I think even at 4 dots and an extra trigger it'll be super common.<br /> <br /> <br /> (I'm glad people seem to like my 4 dots and an extra trigger idea.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair. My personal metric is, could I reasonably see players passing this up for other Merits at the same cost? (I say &quot;reasonably&quot; because a player with no interest in character optimization, or one who is actively opposed to such things might take any Merit over an exp efficient one, even if it doesn't make sense mechanically). If the answer is yes, I don't care if the Merit is &quot;strictly better&quot; than some other Merits. As long as there is still good reason to spend the dots on other things, it's still a choice (if a strong choice) and therefore ok in my book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T08:35:21-08:00","id":828236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=828232#post828232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not all of the kiths are so powerful though. Making it too expensive for the &amp;quot;weaker&amp;quot; kiths could be punishing. Then it becomes a tax on creativity because the merit's cost is determined based on the most &amp;quot;powerful&amp;quot; kiths. I don't think it should be assumed that merit will be used exclusively to take the &amp;quot;best&amp;quot; kiths.</div> </div> </div> </div>On this, I agree with you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T08:40:06-08:00","id":828239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=828232#post828232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not all of the kiths are so powerful though. Making it too expensive for the &amp;quot;weaker&amp;quot; kiths could be punishing. Then it becomes a tax on creativity because the merit's cost is determined based on the most &amp;quot;powerful&amp;quot; kiths. I don't think it should be assumed that merit will be used exclusively to take the &amp;quot;best&amp;quot; kiths.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I would say 4 dots. The &quot;best&quot; Kiths are worth far more than 4 or even 5 dots. There are a very, very small handful of Kiths that 4 dots would seem expensive for, but for the vast majority of Kith choices 4 points is either perfectly reasonable or a serious bargain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T09:01:17-08:00","id":828246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=828239#post828239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is why I would say 4 dots. The &quot;best&quot; Kiths are worth far more than 4 or even 5 dots. There are a very, very small handful of Kiths that 4 dots would seem expensive for, but for the vast majority of Kith choices 4 points is either perfectly reasonable or a serious bargain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your still comparing merits with role playing implications to flat increases to a metric. The role playing requirements act as a mitigating factor. Metrics add little to the experience. The difference in a 6 dice pool becoming a 7 isn't worth noting in most cases except for the actual rolling. It's not part of your character description, an important event in their life, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T09:12:10-08:00","id":828254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=828234#post828234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's fair. My personal metric is, could I reasonably see players passing this up for other Merits at the same cost? (I say &amp;quot;reasonably&amp;quot; because a player with no interest in character optimization, or one who is actively opposed to such things might take any Merit over an exp efficient one, even if it doesn't make sense mechanically). If the answer is yes, I don't care if the Merit is &amp;quot;strictly better&amp;quot; than some other Merits. As long as there is still good reason to spend the dots on other things, it's still a choice (if a strong choice) and therefore ok in my book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok. But it's still a choice at higher dots, too. And it's still a mechanically appealing choice in the case of the vast majority of Kiths. So how does increasing the point cost hurt? The players who don't care about optimizing have the choice either way. They won't even care if they get slightly overcharged for taking one of the weaker Kiths, because the mechanics are largely irrelevant to them, it's the creative option that matters. And players who do care about mechanics won't feel like they're forced to take Dual Kith, because other choices (which might fit <i>their</i> creative vision better) are so mechanically inferior.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T09:14:44-08:00","id":828255,"title":"","content":"That trigger idea was so nifty, I sent it as a recommendation to Dave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T09:19:15-08:00","id":828259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=828246#post828246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your still comparing merits with role playing implications to flat increases to a metric. The role playing requirements act as a mitigating factor. Metrics add little to the experience. The difference in a 6 dice pool becoming a 7 isn't worth noting in most cases except for the actual rolling. It's not part of your character description, an important event in their life, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the mechanics and dice pools don't matter to you, why is paying 4 or 5 dots instead of 3 an issue?<br /> <br /> And all merits come with role-playing implications. You think someone with Striking Looks isn't going to have had seriously different life experiences than someone without it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T09:20:18-08:00","id":828260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=828255#post828255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That trigger idea was so nifty, I sent it as a recommendation to Dave.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's awesome!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T09:29:12-08:00","id":828264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=828254#post828254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok. But it's still a choice at higher dots, too. And it's still a mechanically appealing choice in the case of the vast majority of Kiths. So how does increasing the point cost hurt? The players who don't care about optimizing have the choice either way. They won't even care if they get slightly overcharged for taking one of the weaker Kiths, because the mechanics are largely irrelevant to them, it's the creative option that matters. And players who do care about mechanics won't feel like they're forced to take Dual Kith, because other choices (which might fit <i>their</i> creative vision better) are so mechanically inferior.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, it doesn't. I think 4 dots and maybe a drawback is pretty reasonable. And your extra trigger suggestion would make a fitting drawback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T09:41:22-08:00","id":828273,"title":"","content":"It's far, far more than a single die to a pool in most cases and to present it as such is severely disingenuous. Additional Attributes are huge, not because they give you more dice, but because so many good merits have X Attribute at 3+ as a prerequisite. There are a lot of great merits, both flavorfully and mechanically, and one of the hardest decisions at character creation is always &quot;Which of these merits am I going to lock myself out of, since I can't meet the prereqs for all of them?&quot; A single extra attribute is huge because it drastically cuts down what you have to give up.<br /> <br /> Never failing certain kinds of rolls is huge. Getting exceptional success at 3 dice instead of 5 is huge. That by itself is worth a three dot merit, Inspiring is more broadly useful but can't be used as reliably. Rote is massively powerful, especially when combined with bonus dice or lowered thresholds.<br /> <br /> A Gandharva with Enchanting Performance was one of the most powerful social characters you could make in 1e, because for two glamour you could have both rote and exceptional at 3 on your performance rolls, which could easily lead to 90% odds of an exceptional success.<br /> <br /> It's that kind of synergy, the kind that fundamentally alters how characters interact with the world, which worries people. When you line up bonus on bonus such that the effects multiply and that character can regularly accomplish miracles.<br /> <br /> I've already had to hard ban a combo because one shotting the Arcadian Huntsman from the 1e core book should not be possible for a Wyrd one Changeling with a chair leg.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T10:03:46-08:00","id":828281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=828264#post828264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, it doesn't. I think 4 dots and maybe a drawback is pretty reasonable. And your extra trigger suggestion would make a fitting drawback.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. Well... Ok, then. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T14:03:25-08:00","id":828423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=828259#post828259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the mechanics and dice pools don't matter to you, why is paying 4 or 5 dots instead of 3 an issue?<br /> <br /> And all merits come with role-playing implications. You think someone with Striking Looks isn't going to have had seriously different life experiences than someone without it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mainly because with the way Kiths work, it seems like it would be a character-creation only merit. That means you're deducting a large portion of your starting experiences on a creative/flavor merit. Half of your starting merit points, plus a possibly trigger on top is quite expensive. It's less of an issue if you're playing an established character, but early on I could see it causing some limiting problems. Mainly that it comes at the cost of options for your character in other respects. Devoting what could easily be half of your starting resources on a flavor merit that has effects that may not even be relevant to the character (A Farwalker doesn't have a very practical skill set when in an urban environment, for instance, which is most of the time) and possibly comes bagged with an additional drawback seems extreme for me. Yes, there will be &quot;overpowered choices&quot; but with the sheer amount of kiths there are, and the massive breadth of concepts that they go over, it seems difficult to perfectly balance them all for all situations. You're not always going to be picking your dual-kith in a manner that necessarily synergises. Because of this I don't think you should base the balance of the merit under the assumption that someone's going to try and powergame/munchkin/whatever. <br /> <br /> Second, I'm talking about Merits being more cost-efficient than pumping metrics like attribute points or skills. Striking looks has more role-play potential than just having an additional two dots in persuasion or a dot in presence.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=828273#post828273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's far, far more than a single die to a pool in most cases and to present it as such is severely disingenuous. Additional Attributes are huge, not because they give you more dice, but because so many good merits have X Attribute at 3+ as a prerequisite. There are a lot of great merits, both flavorfully and mechanically, and one of the hardest decisions at character creation is always &quot;Which of these merits am I going to lock myself out of, since I can't meet the prereqs for all of them?&quot; A single extra attribute is huge because it drastically cuts down what you have to give up.<br /> <br /> Never failing certain kinds of rolls is huge. Getting exceptional success at 3 dice instead of 5 is huge. That by itself is worth a three dot merit, Inspiring is more broadly useful but can't be used as reliably. Rote is massively powerful, especially when combined with bonus dice or lowered thresholds.<br /> <br /> A Gandharva with Enchanting Performance was one of the most powerful social characters you could make in 1e, because for two glamour you could have both rote and exceptional at 3 on your performance rolls, which could easily lead to 90% odds of an exceptional success.<br /> <br /> It's that kind of synergy, the kind that fundamentally alters how characters interact with the world, which worries people. When you line up bonus on bonus such that the effects multiply and that character can regularly accomplish miracles.<br /> <br /> I've already had to hard ban a combo because one shotting the Arcadian Huntsman from the 1e core book should not be possible for a Wyrd one Changeling with a chair leg.</div> </div> </div> </div>You act like if you don't have those attributes to start with that you're locked out of them forever. You're also comparing it to 1e, again. This isn't 1e so the comparisons are not entirely accurate in 2e.<br /> <br /> You also assume that the only reason people choose Kiths is to powergame/synergise. That's emphatically not true. Building the game under the assumption that it's being played for min-maxy munchkins I'd think would limit the game. Same thing goes for the merit, because it's possible to minmax it, it must be assumed that that is the only purpose it serves. So, in a way, by treating it as if it were only useful for minmaxing you make it exclusively for minmaxing, as you start basing the costs of acquiring it on that basis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T14:54:37-08:00","id":828445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=828423#post828423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That means you're deducting a large portion of your starting experiences on a creative/flavor merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except it isn't a flavor Merit. It's a Merit with a concrete mechanical bonus to it. It is both a Merit with flavor, and with mechanical value. You might want it for the flavor, not the bonuses, but again, not everything is about what you want.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Devoting what could easily be half of your starting resources on a flavor merit that has effects that may not even be relevant to the character </div> </div> </div>If the bonuses don't matter... why are you even bothering? I mean this in two important ways:<br /> <br /> 1) As per the preview materials examples, changing flavor such as the elemental association of a Kith's powers (fire to electricity, etc.) in a purely cosmetic fashion shouldn't cost you anything. If you just want cosmetic changes, the Dual Kith Merit isn't necessary. You don't buy it just to have cosmetics. You buy it because the changes your character went through are more than cosmetic, they have mechanical weight.<br /> <br /> 2) In any instance of the game, the value of specific traits is variable. Some Kiths are less useful in an urban environment. So are some Skills and mundane Merits. Building a park ranger character of any stripe is kind of useless in a strictly urban game. The rules don't solve this. Talking with your group solves this. The ST needs to communicate the general themes of the chronicle so players know if certain concepts might be less fun because they aren't going to be able to do anything related to the core aspects of that concept. The players need to communicate what interests them to the ST so the ST can design a chronicle to allow the players to explore core aspects of their characters.<br /> <br /> Basically, either the effects don't matter, and you shouldn't be buying Dual Kith just to make a few cosmetic tweaks to your character, and the variability of value of effects based on situation doesn't matter because things still need a cost; you don't reduce the cost of Survival just because it's not going to get used a lot, you discourage concepts that invest heavily in it. Those costs need to work for people that care about the relative costs of things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're not always going to be picking your dual-kith in a manner that necessarily synergises. Because of this I don't think you should base the balance of the merit under the assumption that someone's going to try and powergame/munchkin/whatever. </div> </div> </div>You're making an excluded middle here. The cost needs to reflect that both motivations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You also assume that the only reason people choose Kiths is to powergame/synergise. </div> </div> </div>No. They assume that it is a reason some people choose the Kiths they do; esp. with Dual Kith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T15:39:43-08:00","id":828473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=828423#post828423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mainly because with the way Kiths work, it seems like it would be a character-creation only merit. That means you're deducting a large portion of your starting experiences on a creative/flavor merit. Half of your starting merit points, plus a possibly trigger on top is quite expensive. It's less of an issue if you're playing an established character, but early on I could see it causing some limiting problems. Mainly that it comes at the cost of options for your character in other respects. Devoting what could easily be half of your starting resources on a flavor merit that has effects that may not even be relevant to the character (A Farwalker doesn't have a very practical skill set when in an urban environment, for instance, which is most of the time) and possibly comes bagged with an additional drawback seems extreme for me. Yes, there will be &quot;overpowered choices&quot; but with the sheer amount of kiths there are, and the massive breadth of concepts that they go over, it seems difficult to perfectly balance them all for all situations. You're not always going to be picking your dual-kith in a manner that necessarily synergises. Because of this I don't think you should base the balance of the merit under the assumption that someone's going to try and powergame/munchkin/whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it has been stated that it is not character creation only at present in 2e. And it's not <i>just</i> a creative/flavor meirt; it's a creative/flavor merit that comes with a substantial (though more so in some cases than others) mechanical benefit. And <i>any</i> creative choice you make at character generation is going to cost a portion of those starting resources. If you want to be a veteran cop, you're going to need to invest in some serious merits to make that happen. If you want to be a world class athlete, same deal. You probably don't have enough points to do both, much like you probably don't have enough points to be a Dual Kith and a martial arts master. And that's ok. You can't always get everything you want at character creation. Even if you had to take Dual Kith right away, there's nothing preventing you from taking those other merits later. The last two characters I made, there was no possible way to take all of the merits that I thought would be appropriate for their concepts, so I made some compromises and resolved to buy the missing merits that I thought were necessary as I gained xp. As far as relevance, that applies to plenty of other merits. If you want things for flavor that are unlikely to affect gameplay in any meaningful way most of the time, talk to your ST about getting a price break. (I've handed out free languages and such that were appropriate for character backgrounds, because I knew that they'd likely never or rarely come up in game and I wanted the payer to be able to have them for their concept without getting screwed.) In most cases - the vast majority, Dual Kith is going to be pretty useful and should be an integral, not incidental part of your character; that's worth spending some dots on. And I've never been advocating for perfect balance. Trying for that would involve breaking the Kiths down into lists that are worth different dot values for Dual Kiths; we're not doing that. And I'm not operating under the assumption of power gaming either. <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Even at 4 or 5 dots with a drawback (if you can even call it that), t</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">here are still plenty of Kith pairings that would be easy to power game with.</span></span></span> If I was basing the cost recommendation solely on power gaming, I'd definitely be setting it at 5, with a bigger drawback, and some prereqs. Dealing with those power gaming cases is just going to be a matter of ST adjudication; there's no way around it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=828423#post828423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, I'm talking about Merits being more cost-efficient than pumping metrics like attribute points or skills. Striking looks has more role-play potential than just having an additional two dots in persuasion or a dot in presence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was never talking about that. You accused me of &quot;still comparing merits with role playing implications to flat increases to a metric.&quot; Which I was never doing. I have always been comparing them to other Merits of equivelant cost, and as I stated, <i>all</i> merits should have role-playing implications. I don't have a problem with some merits being better than others, but I do have a slight problem with merits that are <i>way way</i> better than all other merits of that level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5910,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","user":"CSSchulz","date":". 02-11-2016, 08:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T11:39:38-08:00","id":828891,"title":"","content":"As an aside, It's not Character Creation only, but you're encouraged to make it the result of significant story arc if you buy it post-character creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T12:19:02-08:00","id":828914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=828891#post828891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an aside, It's not Character Creation only, but you're encouraged to make it the result of significant story arc if you buy it post-character creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or maybe a Goblin Market purchase with a steep price? But, yeah, it makes sense that it would be a big deal for a character to acquire it during play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T14:31:17-08:00","id":828953,"title":"","content":"Goblin Market was the most common way I saw it justified post-creation back in 1e. Seems legit to keep that up unless the Goblin Markets get a significant redo for 2e in what's on sale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T14:54:49-08:00","id":828963,"title":"","content":"Well, sure, you <i>could</i> just buy it. But considering some Hedge stuff I hope to write, why would I want to fixate just on buying a Kith?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T22:54:43-08:00","id":834280,"title":"","content":"You can also gain it by using the Riddle-kith contract.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thread Reaper <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">\uff1c(\u00b4 \u055e)\u0a0a( \u055e )\uff1e\ufeff</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/377-xanandithras","name":"Xanandithras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar377_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T21:58:11-08:00","id":834833,"title":"","content":"When making courts today I was rather pleased when I realized I could choose to have dual-kith (thematically appropriate kith) as a benefit of getting mantle 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T22:11:45-08:00","id":834836,"title":"","content":"Point of idle curiosity: How does Riddle-Kith interact with characters that already have Dual Kith?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T22:37:40-08:00","id":834846,"title":"","content":"It probably means that you can change one kith, the other or simply go to having one kith for a time; having the Dual-Kith mod already probably means you can have two effective kith changes if you get an Excellent Success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T06:06:35-08:00","id":834975,"title":"","content":"That or you can temporarily stretch to three kiths. Wouldn't let them buy the third permanently though. That way lies madness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T07:14:00-08:00","id":835017,"title":"","content":"Ehhhh it wouldn't be the worst thing in the world.<br /> <br /> A Thusser/Nightsinger/Minstrel is still a person that sings <i>really really well</i>, an Earthbones/Metalflesh/Jeweleyes is still a super tanky earthen person, a Lurker/Larcenist/Palewraith is still a really good thief and house burglar, a Swimmerskin/Waterborn/Nix is still a slippery water person, a Playmate/Truefriend/Dearheart is still the bestest friend you could possibly have, and I'm pretty sure there are other three-kith combinations that I've missed, that don't really change the core changeling's &quot;flavour&quot; at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T07:18:42-08:00","id":835024,"title":"","content":"Oh, three kiths is workable, but if you let someone take a third kith with Riddle Kith, then what happens if they use it again and get another exceptional success? Now they have four kiths. Then five, then six. We need some sort of upper limit, and it makes sense to have that limit be &quot;one actual purchase of the merit&quot;. They can still run around with three kiths indefinitely if they want anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T07:33:37-08:00","id":835036,"title":"","content":"Oh, if that's the case, then I agree completely. I think up to three kiths should be the hard limit. If they want more, that's what epic quests to the Hedge are for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T00:43:50-08:00","id":836900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=828264#post828264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, it doesn't. I think 4 dots and maybe a drawback is pretty reasonable. And your extra trigger suggestion would make a fitting drawback.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. As Heavy Arms mentioned earlier: some of the kiths offer absolutely amazing abilities<br /> <br /> &quot;\u200bYour character gains a free dot in Crafts and a free Specialty in an art form that requires physical strength, such as woodcarving, blacksmithing, or masonry. She may use Strength instead of Wits or Intelligence when creating or appraising items, and gains the Taste Merit (p. XX). Spend a point of Glamour to craft an item related to her Specialty as an instant action instead of an extended action. She needs access to proper tools and materials as usual, but gains automatic successes equal to her Wyrd.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;\u200bWhen establishing a first impression during Social Maneuvering the flowering always moves his impression one step up (p. XX). Spend a point of Glamour to add his Wyrd to any Persuasion, Socialize, or Subterfuge roll made to open a victim\u2019s Doors; an exceptional success on this roll opens Doors equal to his Wyrd, in addition to the normal effects of exceptional success.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;\u200bThe changeling seems somehow larger than she actually is. Add a dot of Presence; this can go above her normal limitation. She gains the four dot version of the Heavy Weapons Fighting Style Merit (p. XX) but it only applies to her unarmed Brawl attacks. Use half the changeling\u2019s Wyrd (rounded up) as the weapon damage when using this Merit. Spend a point of Glamour and an instant action to grows to titanic proportions, adding half her Wyrd dots to her Size for the scene.&quot;<br /> <br /> And some are fairly tame, usually due to a narrow focus<br /> <br /> &quot;The author can never fail an Expression roll to tell or write a story. She automatically achieves one success on such rolls, in addition to the roll results. Also, she can read and interpret anything written in a mortal language.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The changeling gains the Direction Sense Merit (p. XX). The character also reduces the effective level of extreme environments by her Wyrd dots, and adds her Wyrd to her Stamina when calculating how long until she starts taking environmental damage (p. XX). Spend a point of Glamour to add her Wyrd to any Athletics roll to traverse rugged or dangerous terrain.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The swimmerskin can breathe water as easily as air. By spending one Glamour and touching their target\u2019s lips, she can impart that ability for a scene. She can remove this gift at any time. When entirely submerged, the swimmerskin moves at double her normal Speed and does not suffer from environmental exposure due to cold.&quot;<br /> <br /> Gargantuan in particular gives 4 XP of fighting merits, a presence bonus worth 4 XP, a natural weapon worth perhaps 3 XP, and a merit worth perhaps 3 XP.<br /> The extra trigger hurts people who don't min-max much more, due to the fact they will likely have lower wits+resolve. If there was a time for a 7-dot merit, this would be it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Meow! Meow meow meow. Purrrrrr.","edited":{"userid":11326,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11326-misterscruffles","user":"Misterscruffles","date":".  Fixing error in second to last sentence 02-25-2016, 07:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11326-misterscruffles","name":"Misterscruffles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T02:34:59-08:00","id":836940,"title":"","content":"I'm still holding up some hope that the Kiths will get another rules pass considering how disparate the potency of some of them are as-is in the spoiled documents, and that the Merits section either has a few gems hiding in their that haven't been spoiled yet, or gets another significant pass as well.<br /> <br /> As things stand with the spoiled material, I don't think any of my concerns with how Dual Kith played out in 1e are going to be addressed if nothing significant is changed; and bumping it up to 4 dots with a drawback isn't enough.<br /> <br /> There's pretty much nothing I've seen so far that says single-Kith characters aren't going to be left in the dust by Dual Kith characters that focus on the same strengths. Why would you ever spring for Lethal Mien over either just taking Fang and Talon 1 to get lethal attacks for one less XP, or Dual-Kith something like Hunterheart for one more XP and a ton more stuff out of it? If I want to have Presence's cap increased by one, and get a free dot in it, why would I take Arcadian body for four XP vs. Dual Kith with the aforementioned Gargantuan for three?<br /> <br /> The level of char-op available right now is starting to seriously worry me. Two synergistic Kiths that both scale and Wyrd via Dual Kith + Potent Kith... vs. a single Kith character that doesn't even have Wyrd scaling to boost with Potent Kith. Then start tacking on Contracts and it's a newbie trap minefield.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T03:32:20-08:00","id":836950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=836940#post836940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you ever spring for Lethal Mien over either just taking Fang and Talon 1 to get lethal attacks for one less XP, or Dual-Kith something like Hunterheart for one more XP and a ton more stuff out of it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fang and Talon costs a point of glamour per scene, whereas lethal mien is on all the time for free. Additionally it has the bonus effect of granting +1 if you already have a lethal attack option. So if you did go for hunterheart you might decide to get it <i>as well. </i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=836940#post836940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I want to have Presence's cap increased by one, and get a free dot in it, why would I take Arcadian body for four XP vs. Dual Kith with the aforementioned Gargantuan for three?</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I'm pretty sure it stacks. Or maybe you already used both your kiths on boosting <i>other </i>attributes and you want a third to hit six dots at some point. You're looking at all this like you have to pick and choose. No. Take <i>everything. </i>Push it as high as it will go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T07:30:52-08:00","id":837020,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the extra +1 on Lethal mien is really the advantageous part of that merit, given how many lethal unarmed options there are to start. That said, many of the Kiths that benefit from it get equivalent or better mileage out of the same dots in potent kith. But you can stack them, and lethal mien helps the ones who don't have a wyrd scaled natural weapon, like draconics and metalflesh.<br /> <br /> Arcadian Body is interesting, there's no reason not to take it if you're going to spend experience on an attribute increase, but I find there's usually not a whole lot of value to pushing attributes beyond 3 or 4 at the most, with one exception: Dex. With the right merits you can quadruple dip dex for a terrifying martial artist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T07:49:10-08:00","id":837027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The extra trigger hurts people who don't min-max much more, due to the fact they will likely have lower composure+resolve. </div> </div> </div>Clarity breaking points are Wits+Composure.<br /> <br /> It might be more appropriate to underline which kiths need a buff and which need a nerf, rather than messing with Dual-Kith. The merit is not the problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T13:11:32-08:00","id":837180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=836950#post836950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if you did go for hunterheart you might decide to get it <i>as well. </i></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware.<br /> <br /> You're skipping the point to nitpick. The point is not dismissed by the fact that you can buy both, because the point is that you're always better using Dual Kith to get unarmed lethal attacks than other changeling specific options (or even most non-supernatural specific options).<br /> <br /> This makes single Kith characters such a mechanical disadvantage, that it becomes a must have Merit regardless of character concept. Lethal Mien isn't a way to make your unarmed combat character have something to go for besides Dual Kith. It's a secondary concern once you've bought more useful things like Dual Kith.<br /> <br /> &quot;But you can buy everything!&quot; doesn't matter. The core issue that I have is that I want single Kith and Dual Kith PCs to be equally effective characters. As it stands, that's not the case. Dual Kith PCs are always going to be better.<br /> <br /> The fact that you <i>don't have to choose</i> actually makes this worse, because Dual Kith can multiply the bonuses of some other Merits in value.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=837027#post837027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might be more appropriate to underline which kiths need a buff and which need a nerf, rather than messing with Dual-Kith. The merit is not the problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Merit is a problem, even if all the Kiths are better balanced. I've addressed this up-thread.<br /> <br /> As long as Dual Kith PCs are at a massive advantage to other Merit options, the Merit is a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T16:24:55-08:00","id":837280,"title":"","content":"Easy and fast change:<br /> Dual Kith \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <br /> Effect: Your character\u2019s kith is a unique combination of two different kiths. When waking up from sleep, she chooses which kith to gain the benefits of. She can switch which kith she gains the kith benefit of by spending an instant action and a point of either glamor or willpower.<br /> <br /> <i>Edit: Okay this was a terrible idea</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=837027#post837027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clarity breaking points are Wits+Composure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fixed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=837027#post837027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might be more appropriate to underline which kiths need a buff and which need a nerf, rather than messing with Dual-Kith. The merit is not the problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't a problem in changeling 1e, when kith benefits were relatively small, like maybe a point of armor something like that. Most of the 2e kiths give out benefits that synergize well with each other and with regular 2e merits, and many of the benefits are powerful and not available elsewhere (soldier kith), straight up major power boosts (flowering), or give you the equivalent of many XPs worth of merits and attribute boosts (Gargantuan).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Meow! Meow meow meow. Purrrrrr.","edited":{"userid":11326,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11326-misterscruffles","user":"Misterscruffles","date":". 02-26-2016, 12:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11326-misterscruffles","name":"Misterscruffles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T16:30:33-08:00","id":837283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Misterscruffles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=837280#post837280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Easy and fast change:<br /> Dual Kith \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <br /> Effect: Your character\u2019s kith is a unique combination of two different kiths. When waking up from sleep, she chooses which kith to gain the benefits of. She can switch which kith she gains the kith benefit of by spending an instant action and a point of either glamor or willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sorta negates the point of dual-kith... Since you want to be both, not one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T18:09:52-08:00","id":837328,"title":"","content":"It's also extremely overlapping with Riddle-Kith (for the same XP value). Losing the roll and glamour cost, for the inability to pick any Kith you want doesn't seem to be entirely worth it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T18:44:57-08:00","id":837344,"title":"","content":"I genuinely don't think there's anything wrong with Dual-Kith. I do agree some kiths are too appealing and others are too unappealing, and that should be fixed if possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T23:50:51-08:00","id":837408,"title":"","content":"It's page 9 of the thread. The problems with Dual Kith have been expounded on ad nauseum. If you don't see the problems people like me have expressed, I can't see how it is anything other than willfully ignoring it.<br /> <br /> If you actually have a specific question that someone hasn't explained three or four times, please ask away. Otherwise, it doesn't do anything good to essentially dismiss all the people that have had their enjoyment of the game directly - and negatively - impacted by the 1e implementation of it, and who aren't happy that it looks like 2e is keeping it exactly as-is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T06:53:19-08:00","id":837522,"title":"","content":"I don't really intend to argue, I understand that the people who do have a problem with it aren't going to change their minds, so I am throwing my vote for the keeping of the merit. It's a lot easier to disallow the merit in your games than it is for the rest of us to come up with a suitable dot price and requirements for it, were we to homebrew it if it didn't exist, so including it is the best solution for everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T10:57:16-08:00","id":837666,"title":"","content":"What if Dual Kith and Potent Kith were mutually exclusive? Right now taking both is the clear winner from a mechanics standpoint, but what if it was a choice between hyperfocusing one kith or taking two?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T11:20:21-08:00","id":837682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=837522#post837522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really intend to argue, I understand that the people who do have a problem with it aren't going to change their minds, so I am throwing my vote for the keeping of the merit. It's a lot easier to disallow the merit in your games than it is for the rest of us to come up with a suitable dot price and requirements for it, were we to homebrew it if it didn't exist, so including it is the best solution for everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>You might not intend to argue, but by doing so you're just going to pull the same BS that's been pulled for 9 pages?<br /> <br /> Please, cite me one fucking damned post by someone that has a problem with the Merit that actually wants the Merit gone? Because they don't exist. It's an asinine strawman people in-favor of things as-is have made up for reasons I don't understand. I have lost all charity for reading it in any fashion other than flamewar baiting.<br /> <br /> And nobody is asking you to do anything. You're not the lead developer of the game who's job it is to get this right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=837666#post837666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if Dual Kith and Potent Kith were mutually exclusive? Right now taking both is the clear winner from a mechanics standpoint, but what if it was a choice between hyperfocusing one kith or taking two?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would cut down on the worst of it, but I'm not sure it's the best solution. Potent Kith is hardly the only problematic option when stacked with Dual Kith. It could be easier to say that such Merits have to be purchased twice (or powers activated twice) to benefit both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T12:01:43-08:00","id":837697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=837682#post837682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would cut down on the worst of it, but I'm not sure it's the best solution. Potent Kith is hardly the only problematic option when stacked with Dual Kith. It could be easier to say that such Merits have to be purchased twice (or powers activated twice) to benefit both.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good idea, and probably how I would run it in my games either way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T12:16:33-08:00","id":837704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=837682#post837682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And nobody is asking you to do anything. You're not the lead developer of the game who's job it is to get this right.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am adding a voice of support for leaving things as they are, merit-wise. I am nullifying you, statistically speaking. If sufficient people like the merit as-is, the lead developers might tweak the merit in some minor way (such as adding another clarity trigger or increasing the cost one or two dots), but it will be left mostly as it currently is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T12:38:54-08:00","id":837715,"title":"","content":"Fortunately, as one of the writers has already pointed out, game design isn't a popularity contest. Disagreeing with me isn't &quot;nullifying me,&quot; if I'm right that the state of the Merit as-is is too One True Build for the game, and you're disagreeing, because the decision isn't going to be made based on how many people on the forum are on one side or the other. The decision will be made based on who makes points strong enough that they sway the decision making process of the designers.<br /> <br /> Here are the options:<br /> <br /> 1) The designers largely agree with you anyway, and all my concern raising is for naught.<br /> <br /> 2) The designers are on the fence because they see both sides. Those who make strong points matter, those that don't make strong points don't. It's quality, not quantity, that matters to where the designers will finally fall when taking threads like this into account.<br /> <br /> 3) The designers largely agree with me anyway, and I'm preaching to the choir while you're posting for naught.<br /> <br /> Since 1 &amp; 3 don't really impact what will happen, I'm operating on the assumption that 2 is the closest to the truth.<br /> <br /> If all you really want to do, is &quot;nullify&quot; me, just nut up, flame me, take the sanction, and move on with your life. This is a discussion forum, not a &quot;SHUT UP EVERYONE THAT YOU DON'T AGREE WITH&quot; forum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T13:01:03-08:00","id":837725,"title":"","content":"I think you're taking this a bit too personally. I have zero quarrel with you, and I'm speaking to you in a chill way. Why would I want to flame you? I have no feelings whatsoever towards you.<br /> <br /> Popularity does indeed matter, since by and large, the designers want to make a product that is well received and sells well. If more people agree that the merit is fine as it is, it's likely going to remain mostly in its current state, though solid arguments against it might indeed cause it to be tweaked in some minor way (which would be a fine compromise).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T13:30:11-08:00","id":837742,"title":"","content":"I also disagree with dual kith being a must have merit. Its good, no doubt, but their are other equally good merits.<br /> <br /> Mantle, Goblin Vows, Potent Kith, Court Goodwill, and other merits are roughly equal to dual kith, and that's just a taste, we haven't seen all the merits yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T15:24:16-08:00","id":837795,"title":"","content":"I think it's definitely too powerful right now given how the kiths seem to have increased in power in 2e. I mean, when you can buy something worth 8 merits with 3, I think that's an issue (there are many examples of it being worth more than 8, but most aren't as far as I can see) .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T16:07:53-08:00","id":837807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=837725#post837725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're taking this a bit too personally.</div> </div> </div> </div>You said you were trying to nullify me on a one-on-one statistical basis. You made this directly personal by stating you were posting to specifically &quot;nullify&quot; my posts.<br /> <br /> If you don't want people to take things personally, don't make it personal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have zero quarrel with you, and I'm speaking to you in a chill way. Why would I want to flame you? I have no feelings whatsoever towards you. </div> </div> </div>I have no idea how chill you personally feel about this. It's text. And frankly, how chill you are doesn't matter. To an extent, claiming you're being chill just makes what you're saying even worse because if you were doing it out of a heated emotional state, it would be more understandable.<br /> <br /> And you feel enough about me to say that you feel the need to have my opinions, points, and stance silenced. Not just express an alternative, or present a counter-argument, but specifically posting to try to make it so I'm ignored. Which to me, is no different than saying, &quot;fuck you Heavy Arms,&quot; but you at least are smart enough to know that wouldn't fly by the rules.<br /> So you can either go back and look and say to yourself, &quot;You know what, telling someone I'm trying to nullify their opinion from being expressed and listened to by the developer is a pretty dick move,&quot; or you can keep doubling down.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Popularity does indeed matter, since by and large, the designers want to make a product that is well received and sells well. </div> </div> </div>CtL 2e's sales aren't going to suffer if Dual-Kith gets fixed, and the designers know it. That's why one of them expressed stated earlier in the thread that popularity is a bad thing to base design on. Dual-Kith not resulting in massive effectiveness disparities is good for everyone. You've already made it clear that you're not actually so wed to the preview-as-written as you've stated some of the ideas for reducing the problems with it as acceptable; even as you've massively goal-post shifted by trying to present them as &quot;compromises&quot; as if people with a problem with the current rules are asking for more than that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=837742#post837742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also disagree with dual kith being a must have merit. Its good, no doubt, but their are other equally good merits.<br /> <br /> Mantle, Goblin Vows, Potent Kith, Court Goodwill, and other merits are roughly equal to dual kith, and that's just a taste, we haven't seen all the merits yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mantle is on par with MCI, which is better than most Merits, but it still doesn't hold a candle to Dual Kith in terms of effectiveness. <br /> <br /> Goblin Vows aren't in collected previews yet, so if you have a link, please send it, but so far it doesn't seem like they're actually anywhere near Dual Kith.<br /> <br /> Potent Kith is only valuable if you Kith uses Wyrd, and even then the increase is rarely as drastic as a good Dual Kith pick. And of course, Potent Kith is one of the Merits that makes Dual Kith a problem because, as written so far, it's doubly powerful for the right Dual Kiths. You really don't want to face a Dual Kith Hunterheart/Gargantuan in hand to hand combat if they've had a chance to invest significantly in Potent Kith as well (with Hunterheart they'll suffer no penalties for called shots, and with Gargantuan they'll have powerful enough fists to easily deal enough damage to cause Tilts on most hits made with called shots, plus the automatic 1L damage every enemy near them takes along with a dice-penalty).<br /> <br /> Court Goodwill is half Mantle, made up with also being Allies for that Court (but weaker than normal Allies because characters within the Court are much better at blocking you than Status vs. Allies), so this really doesn't get up there.<br /> <br /> And yeah, we haven't seen all the Merits yet. But why should we assume there's some sweet Merits we haven't seen that are on Dual Kith's level when the rest (while fine Merits) aren't?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T16:54:52-08:00","id":837812,"title":"","content":"Goblin Vows is in the latest collection, its under pledges.<br /> <br /> With a Goblin Vow you can get the Dual Kith Merit in exchange for a services.<br /> <br /> Mantle is easily as good as dual kith, you get the effect of Status within your court, you can gain successes x Mantle on contracts when you use Drop the Mask, you gain major benifits for each dot. Mantle 5 Ivory court alone nets you -1 to all die pools to decieve you, a Goblin Vow Merit, 9 again on persuasion rolls, a personal approach which helps protect you from the Gentry and Huntsmen, and you get a 3 dot retainer and once per story you get the value of \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 in either resources, allies, or retainer thanks to the cult of Mithra. That easily equals and exceeds a kith blessing. <br /> <br /> Potent Kith can be wicked and better for certain kiths. with 5 dots and and 2 wyrd a Dearheart can drop anyone's composure by 4, that enough to wipe out the composure of most NPCs, taking out a large chunk of their willpower, their perception, their resistance to many supernatural powers, removing that many doors automatically in social manevuering, and a bunch of other things.<br /> <br /> Think about it Potent Kith just allowed to wipe out a key resistance stat most beings with a touch, no glamour or activation roll needed. If you get Dual Kith instead you get some nice things, no doubt, but you won't be stong enough to wipe out the composure of beings you touch at will, at best you dampen them abit. <br /> <br /> For Soldiers fighting style merits are better, especially if you have hurt locker, because from day to day you could trade 5 dots in each of archery and dirty fighting for 5 dots in falconry and sniper, and the next day trade those 5 dots in each for K9 and Chain fighting.<br /> <br /> Really dual kith is a good merit, but Riddle Kith Contract is better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 02-26-2016, 07:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T16:59:29-08:00","id":837814,"title":"","content":"Mantle is better then Mystery Cult Iniate, its like MCI +. It also gives you access to court contracts, can be used to boost contracts when you Drop the Mask.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T18:13:06-08:00","id":837838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=837812#post837812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Goblin Vows is in the latest collection, its under pledges.<br /> <br /> With a Goblin Vow you can get the Dual Kith Merit in exchange for a services.<br /> <br /> Mantle is easily as good as dual kith, you get the effect of Status within your court, you can gain successes x Mantle on contracts when you use Drop the Mask, you gain major benifits for each dot. Mantle 5 Ivory court alone nets you -1 to all die pools to decieve you, a Goblin Vow Merit, 9 again on persuasion rolls, a personal approach which helps protect you from the Gentry and Huntsmen, and you get a 3 dot retainer and once per story you get the value of \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 in either resources, allies, or retainer thanks to the cult of Mithra. That easily equals and exceeds a kith blessing.<br /> <br /> Potent Kith can be wicked and better for certain kiths. with 5 dots and and 2 wyrd a Dearheart can drop anyone's composure by 4, that enough to wipe out the composure of most NPCs, taking out a large chunk of their willpower, their perception, their resistance to many supernatural powers, removing that many doors automatically in social manevuering, and a bunch of other things.<br /> <br /> Think about it Potent Kith just allowed to wipe out a key resistance stat most beings with a touch, no glamour or activation roll needed. If you get Dual Kith instead you get some nice things, no doubt, but you won't be stong enough to wipe out the composure of beings you touch at will, at best you dampen them abit.<br /> <br /> For Soldiers fighting style merits are better, especially if you have hurt locker, because from day to day you could trade 5 dots in each of archery and dirty fighting for 5 dots in falconry and sniper, and the next day trade those 5 dots in each for K9 and Chain fighting.<br /> <br /> Really dual kith is a good merit, but Riddle Kith Contract is better.</div> </div> </div> </div>And of course, you can stack Goblin Vow, Dual Kith, Mantle, Contracts, Potent Kith, and Professional Training.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Meow! Meow meow meow. Purrrrrr.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11326-misterscruffles","name":"Misterscruffles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T18:30:34-08:00","id":837849,"title":"","content":"Eventually, but not right off the bat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T19:18:15-08:00","id":837867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=837849#post837849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eventually, but not right off the bat.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not immediately, but you can get Dual kith 3, potent kith 5, mantle 2, and some fun contracts off the bat. Professional training 5 and mantle 5 is a &quot;mere&quot; eight XP more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Meow! Meow meow meow. Purrrrrr.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11326-misterscruffles","name":"Misterscruffles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T21:55:20-08:00","id":837938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=837812#post837812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Goblin Vows is in the latest collection, its under pledges.</div> </div> </div> </div>Erm... no it isn't?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mantle is easily as good as dual kith, you get the effect of Status within your court, you can gain successes x Mantle on contracts when you use Drop the Mask, you gain major benifits for each dot. </div> </div> </div>You don't get successes x Mantle when you drop your Mask. You get the highest of rolled successes, Wyrd, or Mantle on Contracts when the number of successes matters to activation.<br /> <br /> And &quot;major&quot; benefits for each dot is over stating things a tad. The guidelines are:<br /> <br /> 1:<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Benefits may be a one-dot merit pertaining to the court's ideals, +1 to a skill, or a -1 penalty to a specific type of roll made against the courtier.<br /> 2: </span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Courtiers gain a dot of the Goblin Vow merit related to their court.<br /> 3: </span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Courtiers may take 9 again in a skill, a two-dot merit, +2 on skills vs. specific situations, or +1 to defense, initiative, speed, or armor.<br /> 4: </span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Courtiers gain a Personal Approach related to how they fulfill the ideals and story of the court.<br /> 5: </span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Benefits may be a three-dot merit, reroll failures of a particular skill, +1 to Health or Willpower, or a major advantage not reflected in game traits.<br /> <br /> <br /> So it's the equivalent of ~7 Merit dots + a Personal Approach in &quot;major advantages&quot;, for 5 Merit dots on top of the other effects, which is pretty close to MCI since it suggests 10 Merit dots worth of bonuses by 5 dots (1 dot Merit, 1 dot Merit, 2 dot Merit, 3 dot Merit, 3 dot Merit).</span></span><br /> <br /> Is it better than MCI? Yes. But not by a huge degree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Think about it Potent Kith just allowed to wipe out a key resistance stat most beings with a touch, no glamour or activation roll needed. If you get Dual Kith instead you get some nice things, no doubt, but you won't be stong enough to wipe out the composure of beings you touch at will, at best you dampen them abit. </div> </div> </div>These things aren't mutually exclusive, and there are plenty of Kiths that have good synergy with Dearhearts that boost your efforts in Social Maneuvering, such as the ones that improve your Impressions so you don't have to force Doors to go quickly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For Soldiers fighting style merits are better, especially if you have hurt locker, because from day to day you could trade 5 dots in each of archery and dirty fighting for 5 dots in falconry and sniper, and the next day trade those 5 dots in each for K9 and Chain fighting. </div> </div> </div>Sorta? Again, this is ignoring any sort of synergies you can get with Dual Kith. 3 more dots of Fighting Style dots to move around is great, but they're probably not going to be as potent as what many of the combat Kith Blessings can grant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Really dual kith is a good merit, but Riddle Kith Contract is better. </div> </div> </div>Except it isn't? Switching Kiths is nice, but it doesn't let you stack to synergistic ones together. The exceptional success of Riddle Kith is... temporary access to Dual-Kith. Riddle-Kith is also a 3 dot Contract, so it isn't like it's cheaper, and there's the Glamour/rolls/Clarity costs to deal with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T22:18:41-08:00","id":837943,"title":"","content":"Compare:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>1st edition Flowering</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seductive Fragrance: her skin, hair and breath carries the aroma of unknown blossoms from places unseen, the promise of pleasures unknown. Her bouquet seduces and lulls in equal measure. She gains the benefit of the 9 again rule on dice pools including Persuasion, Socialize and Subterfuge.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2nd edition Flowering</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blessing: \u200bWhen establishing a first impression during Social Maneuvering the flowering always moves his impression one step up. Spend a point of Glamour to add his Wyrd to any Persuasion, Socialize, or Subterfuge roll made to open a victim\u2019s Doors; an exceptional success on this roll opens Doors equal to his Wyrd, in addition to the normal effects of exceptional success.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>1st edition Gargantuan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spurious Stature: once a day, the changeling can grow to colossal size. The player player spends a point of Glamour, and adds the changeling\u2019s Wyrd score to her size for the rest of the scene. This supplies temporary Health dots (see the World of Darkness Rulebook, p. 175). Returning to normal size is painful, as if the changeling\u2019s skin is unable to contain the character\u2019s stature, and when she regains her normal height, the character takes one point of lethal damage.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2nd edition Gargantuan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThe changeling seems somehow larger than she actually is. Add a dot of Presence; this can go above her normal limitation. She gains the four dot version of the Heavy Weapons Fighting Style Merit (p. XX) but it only applies to her unarmed Brawl attacks. Use half the changeling\u2019s Wyrd (rounded up) as the weapon damage when using this Merit. Spend a point of Glamour and an instant action to grows to titanic proportions, adding half her Wyrd dots to her Size for the scene.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>1st edition Soldier</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blade Lore: living and breathing the lore of the blade, the Soldiers of the goblin hosts find it easy to master any weapon that carries an edge. A Soldier is considered to have a Weaponry specialization with any weapon that carries an edge, no matter what it is. This can\u2019t stack with other specializations the changeling may learn.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2nd edition Soldier</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A soldiers is adaptable. She can ignore any Attribute or Skill prerequisites for Fighting Style Merits. With a full night\u2019s sleep, she can exchange any dots in a Fighting Style Merit for the same number of dots in other Fighting Style Merits. When another character uses a Fighting Style, Spend a point of Glamour to know which. A soldier does not take Initiative penalties from weapons, and reduces Defense penalties from armor by half her Wyrd, rounded up.</div> </div> </div> </div>1st edition dual kith =/= 2nd edition dual kith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Meow! Meow meow meow. Purrrrrr.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11326-misterscruffles","name":"Misterscruffles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T22:56:33-08:00","id":837950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/824985-multi-kith-merit-in-2e?p=837938#post837938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Erm... no it isn't?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1EioGQle5FQ14d3AIXGAXJA8AXbANuj-vwdgQS84eub4/mobilebasic\" target=\"_blank\">Here.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T00:00:46-08:00","id":837967,"title":"","content":"Thank you.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, as to compare Goblin Vows:<br /> <br /> There's a rather large trade-off with them that constitutes a huge drawback in comparison to Dual Kith, as they have both a favor you need to do, and consequences for not fulfilling your part. There's also an issue with Goblin Vows still needing to be within the purview of whatever you're dealing with, which also has to be available to you when you want to make the Vow. Medial and Major favors, which are going to be what you need to take to rival Dual Kith, are either going to last long enough for them to be put at risk, or you're going to drop the time on them and thus their duration.<br /> <br /> Goblin Vows are really nice for emergency boosts, or flexibility when planning something, but trying to run around for a season with a 3 dot Merit, or +7 dice to something, means a whole season where you have to follow through with something. A single night where you accidentally got sucked into a party, and didn't get around to your nightly task before sunrise? Oh well. Whatever the sanction is, now gets slapped on you for a season and you have the Oathbreaker Condition to deal with.<br /> <br /> Sure, you can theoretically make multiple Vows for a butt-load of power, but that just increases the odds of breaking them; just like any other form of Pledging.<br /> <br /> So Goblin Vows fails to stack up for a few reasons. It has major drawbacks, increasing dots only helps ensure you can find something to make the Vow you want to make without increasing potency and you get a free dot for Mantle 2 anyway, and doesn't have the reliability that Kith Blessings do.<br /> <br /> Not saying Goblin Vows are bad as written. I like them really. But they're still not a Merit that's begging for every PC to slap dots into. A Mantle 2 PC is going to cover this well enough for most PCs (esp. since the Mantle Goblin Vow category is going to be something the Court has relative access to in order to make sense).<br /> <br /> Though I'll acknowledge there seems to be a very different valuing in terms of character flexibility. Goblin Vows, Riddle-Kith, and Solider are all ways for characters to gain a specialization without committing to it long term. They let changelings boost themselves in one area as they need, and switch another day. Which is sweet, but it's fiddly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}